  {
    "id": "T1Q2",
    "type": "hotspot-dropdown",
    "stem": "As a Fabric administrator, you need a logical Research classification for the Contoso workspaces and their items in OneLake catalog. Keep their capacity assignments unchanged. Which grouping and documented current management route should you use?",
    "blanks": [
      {
        "label": "Grouping method:",
        "options": [
          "Capacity",
          "Domain",
          "Tenant"
        ],
        "answer": "Domain"
      },
      {
        "label": "Tool:",
        "options": [
          "OneLake catalog > Govern > Domains",
          "Capacity settings",
          "Microsoft Entra admin center"
        ],
        "answer": "OneLake catalog > Govern > Domains"
      }
    ],
    "semanticVisuals": [],
    "caseStudy": "cs_contoso",
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q2",
    "sourceId": "T1Q2",
    "gradingEnabled": true,
    "scientificStatus": "APPROVED_CORRECTED",
    "r10Status": "CORRECTION_PROPOSED",
    "reviewNote": "Replaced legacy admin route with the documented current domain management path.",
    "remaining": "",
    "explanation": "Use a Domain and manage it in OneLake catalog > Govern > Domains. Workspace assignment associates its items with the domain. Capacity is a compute assignment and the candidate keeps it unchanged. Tenant is the organization boundary, not the requested department classification. Entra admin center does not create Fabric domains.",
    "answer": null,
    "officialAnswer": "",
    "original": {
      "type": "hotspot-dropdown",
      "officialAnswer": "",
      "blanks": [
        {
          "label": "Grouping method:",
          "options": [
            "Capacity",
            "Domain",
            "Tenant"
          ],
          "answer": "Domain"
        },
        {
          "label": "Tool:",
          "options": [
            "OneLake data hub",
            "The Fabric Admin portal",
            "The Microsoft Entra admin center"
          ],
          "answer": "The Fabric Admin portal"
        }
      ],
      "stem": "You need to recommend a solution to group the Research division workspaces.\nWhat should you include in the recommendation? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.",
      "explanation": "**Domain — The Fabric Admin portal.**\n\nThe requirement is that *\"the Research division workspaces must be grouped together logically to support OneLake data hub filtering based on the department name.\"* That is the textbook definition of a **domain**: *\"a domain is a way of logically grouping together all the data in an organization that is relevant to a particular area or field.\"* Once workspaces are assigned to a domain, the OneLake data hub gains a domain filter — exactly the behaviour asked for.\n\n- **Capacity** groups workspaces for *billing and compute*, not for data-hub filtering.\n- **Tenant** is the whole organization; it is not a grouping you create.\n\nDomains are created and managed by the Fabric admin (or a domain admin) in **Settings → Admin portal → Domains** — i.e. the **Fabric Admin portal**. The OneLake data hub is where you *consume* the resulting filter, not where you define the grouping, and the Microsoft Entra admin center manages identity, not Fabric content."
    },
    "sourceVisualReferences": {
      "exhibits": [
