  {
    "id": "T1Q6",
    "type": "hotspot-dropdown",
    "stem": "You need to create a DAX measure to calculate the average overall satisfaction score.\nHow should you complete the DAX code? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.",
    "blanks": [
      {
        "label": "CALCULATE ( ______",
        "options": [
          "AVERAGE('Survey'[Response Value]),",
          "AVERAGEA('Question'[Question Text]),",
          "AVERAGEX(VALUES('Survey'[Customer Key]),"
        ],
        "answer": "AVERAGE('Survey'[Response Value]),"
      },
      {
        "label": "______  (second CALCULATE argument)",
        "options": [
          "LastCurrentDate,",
          "NumberOfMonths,",
          "Period,"
        ],
        "answer": "Period,"
      }
    ],
    "semanticVisuals": [
      {
        "kind": "code",
        "title": "Original DAX template — fill both dropdown blanks",
        "language": "dax",
        "content": "Rolling 12 Overall Satisfaction =\nVAR NumberOfMonths = 12\nVAR LastCurrentDate = MAX ( 'Date'[Date] )\nVAR Period = DATESINPERIOD ( 'Date'[Date], LastCurrentDate,\n    - NumberOfMonths, MONTH )\nVAR Result =\n    CALCULATE (\n        [Dropdown 1: aggregate expression],\n        [Dropdown 2: period filter],\n        'Survey Question'[Question Title] = \"Overall Satisfaction\"\n    )\nRETURN\n    Result"
      }
    ],
    "caseStudy": "cs_litware",
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q6",
    "sourceId": "T1Q6",
    "gradingEnabled": false,
    "scientificStatus": "BLOCKED_SOURCE",
    "r10Status": "AMBIGUOUS",
    "reviewNote": "Withheld grading for mismatched model schema and undefined response weighting.",
    "remaining": "Complete current primary-doc section review, source screenshot/case checks and native fixture where material; then independently challenge every final option.",
    "explanation": "**`AVERAGE('Survey'[Response Value]),` — `Period,`**\n\nThe measure is a rolling-12-month average, and the variables above the blanks do all the date work:\n\n```dax\nRolling 12 Overall Satisfaction =\nVAR NumberOfMonths = 12\nVAR LastCurrentDate = MAX ( 'Date'[Date] )\nVAR Period = DATESINPERIOD ( 'Date'[Date], LastCurrentDate, - NumberOfMonths, MONTH )\nVAR Result =\n  CALCULATE (\n    <blank 1>\n    <blank 2>\n    'Survey Question'[Question Title] = \"Overall Satisfaction\"\n  )\nRETURN Result\n```\n\n**Blank 1 — the expression `CALCULATE` evaluates.** The satisfaction score is the numeric column `'Survey'[Response Value]`, so `AVERAGE('Survey'[Response Value])` is the whole calculation.\n- `AVERAGEA('Question'[Question Text])` averages a *text* column. `AVERAGEA` coerces text to 0, so this returns 0 — meaningless here.\n- `AVERAGEX(VALUES('Survey'[Customer Key]),` is syntactically incomplete as written (`AVERAGEX` needs a second `<expression>` argument), and averaging customer keys is not the ask.\n\n**Blank 2 — the filter argument.** `CALCULATE` takes filters after the expression, and `Period` is already the `DATESINPERIOD(...)` table covering the last 12 months. Passing it filters the calculation to that window.\n- `LastCurrentDate` is a single date (scalar), which would collapse the result to one day.\n- `NumberOfMonths` is the integer 12 — not a filter at all.",
    "answer": null,
    "officialAnswer": "",
    "original": {
      "type": "hotspot-dropdown",
      "officialAnswer": "",
      "blanks": [
        {
          "label": "CALCULATE ( ______",
          "options": [
            "AVERAGE('Survey'[Response Value]),",
            "AVERAGEA('Question'[Question Text]),",
            "AVERAGEX(VALUES('Survey'[Customer Key]),"
          ],
          "answer": "AVERAGE('Survey'[Response Value]),"
        },
        {
          "label": "______  (second CALCULATE argument)",
          "options": [
            "LastCurrentDate,",
            "NumberOfMonths,",
            "Period,"
          ],
          "answer": "Period,"
        }
      ],
      "stem": "You need to create a DAX measure to calculate the average overall satisfaction score.\nHow should you complete the DAX code? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.",
      "explanation": "**`AVERAGE('Survey'[Response Value]),` — `Period,`**\n\nThe measure is a rolling-12-month average, and the variables above the blanks do all the date work:\n\n```dax\nRolling 12 Overall Satisfaction =\nVAR NumberOfMonths = 12\nVAR LastCurrentDate = MAX ( 'Date'[Date] )\nVAR Period = DATESINPERIOD ( 'Date'[Date], LastCurrentDate, - NumberOfMonths, MONTH )\nVAR Result =\n  CALCULATE (\n    <blank 1>\n    <blank 2>\n    'Survey Question'[Question Title] = \"Overall Satisfaction\"\n  )\nRETURN Result\n```\n\n**Blank 1 — the expression `CALCULATE` evaluates.** The satisfaction score is the numeric column `'Survey'[Response Value]`, so `AVERAGE('Survey'[Response Value])` is the whole calculation.\n- `AVERAGEA('Question'[Question Text])` averages a *text* column. `AVERAGEA` coerces text to 0, so this returns 0 — meaningless here.\n- `AVERAGEX(VALUES('Survey'[Customer Key]),` is syntactically incomplete as written (`AVERAGEX` needs a second `<expression>` argument), and averaging customer keys is not the ask.\n\n**Blank 2 — the filter argument.** `CALCULATE` takes filters after the expression, and `Period` is already the `DATESINPERIOD(...)` table covering the last 12 months. Passing it filters the calculation to that window.\n- `LastCurrentDate` is a single date (scalar), which would collapse the result to one day.\n- `NumberOfMonths` is the integer 12 — not a filter at all."
    },
    "sourceVisualReferences": {
