    "semanticVisuals": [],
    "caseStudy": "cs_litware",
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q8",
    "sourceId": "T1Q8",
    "gradingEnabled": false,
    "scientificStatus": "R10_APPROVAL_CANDIDATE_NOT_REVALIDATED",
    "r10Status": "APPROVED",
    "reviewNote": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "Two lines in the case study decide this: *\"Whenever possible, the data engineers will use low-code tools for data ingestion\"* and *\"Data will be loaded without transformation in one area of the AnalyticsPOC data store.\"*\n\nA **dataflow** (Dataflow Gen2) is Fabric's low-code ingestion tool — Power Query in the browser, with a data destination — so it is the one that honours the stated preference.\n\n- **A** – a stored procedure is T-SQL code, and it cannot reach the external CRM system in the first place.\n- **B** – a KQL activity targets a KQL database for real-time/log analytics; the source here is a nightly CRM extract, and the destination is a lakehouse.\n- **C** – a Spark notebook would work technically, but it is the *pro-code* option, which the requirement explicitly deprioritises.",
    "answer": "D",
    "officialAnswer": "D",
    "original": {
      "type": "mcq",
      "officialAnswer": "D",
      "answer": "D",
      "stem": "What should you recommend using to ingest the customer data into the data store in the AnalyticsPOC workspace?",
      "options": [
        {
          "letter": "A",
          "text": "a stored procedure",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "B",
          "text": "a pipeline that contains a KQL activity",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "C",
          "text": "a Spark notebook",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "D",
          "text": "a dataflow",
          "mostVoted": true
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "Two lines in the case study decide this: *\"Whenever possible, the data engineers will use low-code tools for data ingestion\"* and *\"Data will be loaded without transformation in one area of the AnalyticsPOC data store.\"*\n\nA **dataflow** (Dataflow Gen2) is Fabric's low-code ingestion tool — Power Query in the browser, with a data destination — so it is the one that honours the stated preference.\n\n- **A** – a stored procedure is T-SQL code, and it cannot reach the external CRM system in the first place.\n- **B** – a KQL activity targets a KQL database for real-time/log analytics; the source here is a nightly CRM extract, and the destination is a lakehouse.\n- **C** – a Spark notebook would work technically, but it is the *pro-code* option, which the requirement explicitly deprioritises."
    },
