    "id": "T1Q13",
    "type": "mcq",
    "stem": "You are the administrator of a Fabric workspace that contains a lakehouse named Lakehouse1. Lakehouse1 contains the following tables:\nTable1: A Delta table created by using a shortcut\nTable2: An external table created by using Spark\nTable3: A managed table -\nYou plan to connect to Lakehouse1 by using its SQL endpoint.\nWhat will you be able to do after connecting to Lakehouse1?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Read Table3."
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Update the data Table3."
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Read Table2."
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Update the data in Table1."
      }
    ],
    "semanticVisuals": [],
    "caseStudy": null,
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q13",
    "sourceId": "T1Q13",
    "gradingEnabled": false,
    "scientificStatus": "R10_APPROVAL_CANDIDATE_NOT_REVALIDATED",
    "r10Status": "APPROVED",
    "reviewNote": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "Two facts decide every option here.\n\n**1. The SQL analytics endpoint is read-only.** The doc states it plainly: *\"The SQL analytics endpoint … is a read-only experience. It doesn't support the full T-SQL surface area of a Fabric warehouse.\"* You can `SELECT`, create views and apply security, but you cannot `INSERT`, `UPDATE` or `DELETE`. That kills **B** (update Table3) and **D** (update Table1) regardless of table kind.\n\n**2. The endpoint only surfaces managed Delta tables in the lakehouse `Tables` area.** Spark **external** tables are registered in the metastore with their own `LOCATION`; they appear in Lakehouse explorer but are *not* projected into the SQL analytics endpoint. That kills **C**.\n\n**Table3 is a managed table**, so it is exposed and readable — **A**. (Table1, the shortcut, is also readable, but the option offered for it asks to *update* it, which is not allowed.)",
    "answer": "A",
    "officialAnswer": "A",
    "original": {
      "type": "mcq",
      "officialAnswer": "A",
      "answer": "A",
      "stem": "You are the administrator of a Fabric workspace that contains a lakehouse named Lakehouse1. Lakehouse1 contains the following tables:\nTable1: A Delta table created by using a shortcut\nTable2: An external table created by using Spark\nTable3: A managed table -\nYou plan to connect to Lakehouse1 by using its SQL endpoint.\nWhat will you be able to do after connecting to Lakehouse1?",
      "options": [
        {
          "letter": "A",
          "text": "Read Table3.",
          "mostVoted": true
        },
        {
          "letter": "B",
