          "letter": "C",
          "text": "Read Table2.",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "D",
          "text": "Update the data in Table1.",
          "mostVoted": false
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "Two facts decide every option here.\n\n**1. The SQL analytics endpoint is read-only.** The doc states it plainly: *\"The SQL analytics endpoint … is a read-only experience. It doesn't support the full T-SQL surface area of a Fabric warehouse.\"* You can `SELECT`, create views and apply security, but you cannot `INSERT`, `UPDATE` or `DELETE`. That kills **B** (update Table3) and **D** (update Table1) regardless of table kind.\n\n**2. The endpoint only surfaces managed Delta tables in the lakehouse `Tables` area.** Spark **external** tables are registered in the metastore with their own `LOCATION`; they appear in Lakehouse explorer but are *not* projected into the SQL analytics endpoint. That kills **C**.\n\n**Table3 is a managed table**, so it is exposed and readable — **A**. (Table1, the shortcut, is also readable, but the option offered for it asks to *update* it, which is not allowed.)"
