      ],
      "explanation": "The Fabric `PREDICT` function is a **Spark** construct. Microsoft documents three ways to call it, and the two that are offered here are **PySpark** and **Spark SQL**:\n\n- the low-code **PREDICT wizard** in the ML model UI,\n- the **Spark DataFrame API** from a notebook — `MLFlowTransformer(...)` in **PySpark** (and Scala/R),\n- **Spark SQL**, by registering the model as a Spark SQL UDF and calling it in a `SELECT`.\n\n- **A T-SQL** – Fabric notebooks do not run T-SQL, and `PREDICT` in a warehouse is a different, unrelated feature (it is not how you score a model registered in a Fabric workspace from a notebook).\n- **B DAX** – a semantic-model query language. It has no model-scoring function and cannot run in a notebook.\n\nThe notebook language set is PySpark, Scala Spark, Spark SQL and SparkR — of the four options, only C and D are in it."
    },
