    "explanation": "**`display(df)`** is the Fabric notebook function that renders the rich output widget — and that widget is where the **Chart view** toggle lives. The doc: *\"You can use the `display` function … on Spark DataFrames … to produce the rich dataframe table view and chart view.\"*\n\n- **B `show`** – `df.show()` prints a plain ASCII table to the cell output. No widget, no chart view.\n- **A `displayHTML`** – renders an arbitrary HTML string. It is unrelated to DataFrames and gives you no chart view.\n- **C `write`** – `df.write` persists the DataFrame to storage; it produces no output at all.",
