    },
    "semanticVisuals": [
      {
        "kind": "code",
        "title": "Original DAX query with draggable target markers",
        "language": "dax",
        "content": "[Target 1]\n    VAR _SalesSince = DATE (2023, 12, 01)\n[Target 2]\n    FILTER (\n        [Target 3] (Store, Store[Name], Store[OpenDate]),\n        Store[OpenDate] >= _SalesSince\n    )"
      }
    ],
    "caseStudy": null,
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q18",
    "sourceId": "T1Q18",
    "gradingEnabled": false,
    "scientificStatus": "R10_APPROVAL_CANDIDATE_NOT_REVALIDATED",
    "r10Status": "APPROVED",
    "reviewNote": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "**DEFINE — EVALUATE — SUMMARIZE.** A DAX *query* (the kind the XMLA endpoint executes, as opposed to a measure) has a fixed skeleton:\n\n```dax\nDEFINE\n    VAR _SalesSince = DATE ( 2023, 12, 01 )\nEVALUATE\n    FILTER (\n        SUMMARIZE ( Store, Store[Name], Store[OpenDate] ),\n        Store[OpenDate] >= _SalesSince\n    )\n```\n\n- **`DEFINE`** introduces the optional definition block. It is *\"used to define entities that exist only for the duration of the query\"* — here the `VAR _SalesSince`. It must come first, and a query may have at most one.\n- **`EVALUATE`** is mandatory and introduces the table expression that the query returns: *\"the EVALUATE statement … contains a table expression to be evaluated and returned.\"*\n- **`SUMMARIZE`** is the missing function inside `FILTER`. `FILTER(<table>, <condition>)` needs a *table* as its first argument, and `SUMMARIZE(Store, Store[Name], Store[OpenDate])` produces the two-column table of stores that the filter then narrows to those opened on or after 1 December 2023.\n\n- **`TABLE`** is not a DAX query keyword (it is a `DEFINE TABLE` sub-clause, which does not fit any of these slots).\n- **`FILTER`** is already printed in the code, so it is a distractor in the Values pane.",
    "answer": null,
    "officialAnswer": "",
    "original": {
      "type": "dragdrop",
      "officialAnswer": "",
      "drag": {
        "items": [
          "DEFINE",
          "EVALUATE",
          "FILTER",
          "SUMMARIZE",
          "TABLE"
        ],
        "reuse": true,
        "targets": [
          {
            "label": "Line 1 (before  VAR _SalesSince = DATE (2023, 12, 01) )",
            "answer": "DEFINE"
          },
          {
            "label": "Line 3 (before  FILTER( )",
            "answer": "EVALUATE"
          },
          {
            "label": "Inside FILTER:  ______ (Store, Store[Name], Store[OpenDate]),",
            "answer": "SUMMARIZE"
          }
        ]
      },
      "stem": "You have a Fabric tenant that contains a semantic model. The model contains data about retail stores.\nYou need to write a DAX query that will be executed by using the XMLA endpoint. The query must return a table of stores that have opened since\nDecember 1, 2023.\nHow should you complete the DAX expression? To answer, drag the appropriate values to the correct targets. Each value may be used once, more\nthan once, or not at all. You may need to drag the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.",
      "explanation": "**DEFINE — EVALUATE — SUMMARIZE.** A DAX *query* (the kind the XMLA endpoint executes, as opposed to a measure) has a fixed skeleton:\n\n```dax\nDEFINE\n    VAR _SalesSince = DATE ( 2023, 12, 01 )\nEVALUATE\n    FILTER (\n        SUMMARIZE ( Store, Store[Name], Store[OpenDate] ),\n        Store[OpenDate] >= _SalesSince\n    )\n```\n\n- **`DEFINE`** introduces the optional definition block. It is *\"used to define entities that exist only for the duration of the query\"* — here the `VAR _SalesSince`. It must come first, and a query may have at most one.\n- **`EVALUATE`** is mandatory and introduces the table expression that the query returns: *\"the EVALUATE statement … contains a table expression to be evaluated and returned.\"*\n- **`SUMMARIZE`** is the missing function inside `FILTER`. `FILTER(<table>, <condition>)` needs a *table* as its first argument, and `SUMMARIZE(Store, Store[Name], Store[OpenDate])` produces the two-column table of stores that the filter then narrows to those opened on or after 1 December 2023.\n\n- **`TABLE`** is not a DAX query keyword (it is a `DEFINE TABLE` sub-clause, which does not fit any of these slots).\n- **`FILTER`** is already printed in the code, so it is a distractor in the Values pane."
    },
    "sourceVisualReferences": {
