    "explanation": "Read the **Column statistics** panel in the exhibit for `pickupLongitude`:\n\n| Statistic | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| Count | **1000** |\n| Error count | 0 |\n| Null count | **0** |\n| Distinct count | **935** |\n| Unique count | **871** |\n| NaN count | 0 |\n\n**A — the column has duplicate values.** 1,000 values but only **935 distinct** ones, so 65 of them repeat a value already seen. Duplicates, confirmed.\n\n- **B** – the query returns **2,000** rows but `Count` is **1,000**. Power Query profiles only the **top 1,000 rows** by default (the status bar offers \"Column profiling based on top 1000 rows\"), so not all rows are profiled.\n- **C** – `Null count` is **0** and `Error count` is **0**. No missing values.\n- **D** – 935 is the **Distinct count** (how many different values exist), not how many occur exactly once. The count of values occurring only once is the **Unique count**, which is **871**.",
