        "text": "the C1 settings"
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "the Tenant1 settings"
      }
    ],
    "semanticVisuals": [],
    "caseStudy": null,
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q20",
    "sourceId": "T1Q20",
    "gradingEnabled": false,
    "scientificStatus": "R10_APPROVAL_CANDIDATE_NOT_REVALIDATED",
    "r10Status": "APPROVED",
    "reviewNote": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "The XMLA endpoint has **two** switches, and the question asks which to modify *first* to get **read-write**:\n\n| Where | Setting | Default |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Tenant settings | *Allow XMLA endpoints and Analyze in Excel with on-premises datasets* | **Enabled** |\n| **Capacity settings** | **XMLA Endpoint** — Off / **Read Only** / Read Write | **Read Only** |\n\nThe tenant switch is already on by default, so nothing needs changing there. The capacity switch defaults to **Read Only**, which is precisely what blocks read-write access. The doc's instruction is *\"In the capacity settings, expand the Power BI workloads, and under XMLA Endpoint select Read Write.\"*\n\n- **A / B** – there is no XMLA setting on a dataset or on a workspace.\n- **D** – the tenant setting governs whether XMLA endpoints may be used *at all*; it is on by default and does not control read-write.",
    "answer": "C",
    "officialAnswer": "C",
    "original": {
      "type": "mcq",
      "officialAnswer": "C",
      "answer": "C",
      "stem": "You have a Fabric tenant named Tenant1 that contains a workspace named WS1. WS1 uses a capacity named C1 and contains a dataset named\nDS1.\nYou need to ensure read-write access to DS1 is available by using XMLA endpoint.\nWhat should be modified first?",
      "options": [
        {
          "letter": "A",
          "text": "the DS1 settings",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "B",
          "text": "the WS1 settings",
          "mostVoted": false
