    "remaining": "Complete current primary-doc section review, source screenshot/case checks and native fixture where material; then independently challenge every final option.",
    "explanation": "Three things have to be true before a user can build and publish a custom Direct Lake model from an external tool such as Tabular Editor:\n\n- **A — Tenant settings → *Allow XMLA Endpoints and Analyze in Excel with on-premises datasets* = Enabled.** This is the org-wide master switch for XMLA connectivity. With it off, nothing below matters.\n- **D — Capacity settings → *XMLA Endpoint* = Read Write.** The capacity default is **Read Only**, which permits external tools to connect and query but not to deploy. Publishing a model requires **Read Write**.\n- **E — Tenant settings → *Users can create Fabric items* = Enabled.** A Direct Lake semantic model is a Fabric item, so users need the right to create Fabric items at all.\n\nRejected:\n- **B** *Allow Azure AD guest users…* – about external identities, irrelevant here, and granting it would violate least privilege.\n- **C** *Users can edit data model in the Power BI service* – enables the **web** modelling experience. The requirement is **external tools** over XMLA, which is a different path.\n- **F** *Publish to Web* – publishes reports anonymously to the public internet. Unrelated, and a serious least-privilege violation.",
    "answer": "ADE",
    "officialAnswer": "ADE",
