    "id": "T1Q22",
    "type": "mcq",
    "stem": "You are creating a semantic model in Microsoft Power BI Desktop.\nYou plan to make bulk changes to the model by using the Tabular Model Definition Language (TMDL) extension for Microsoft Visual Studio Code.\nYou need to save the semantic model to a file.\nWhich file format should you use?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "PBIP"
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "PBIX"
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "PBIT"
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "PBIDS"
      }
    ],
    "semanticVisuals": [],
    "caseStudy": null,
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q22",
    "sourceId": "T1Q22",
    "gradingEnabled": false,
    "scientificStatus": "R10_APPROVAL_CANDIDATE_NOT_REVALIDATED",
    "r10Status": "APPROVED",
    "reviewNote": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "**PBIP — Power BI Project.** Saving as a project writes the report and the semantic model out as **plain-text folders on disk** instead of one binary file, which is what makes the model definition editable in VS Code and diffable in Git. The semantic model folder is where the **TMDL** files live (`definition/tables/*.tmdl`), so the TMDL extension for VS Code can open and bulk-edit them.\n\n- **B PBIX** – the standard Power BI Desktop file. It is a single binary archive; external text tooling cannot edit the model inside it.\n- **C PBIT** – a Power BI *template*: a PBIX without the data. Still binary, still not text-editable.\n- **D PBIDS** – a tiny \"data source\" connection file used to start a new report against a given source. It contains no model at all.",
    "answer": "A",
    "officialAnswer": "A",
    "original": {
      "type": "mcq",
      "officialAnswer": "A",
      "answer": "A",
      "stem": "You are creating a semantic model in Microsoft Power BI Desktop.\nYou plan to make bulk changes to the model by using the Tabular Model Definition Language (TMDL) extension for Microsoft Visual Studio Code.\nYou need to save the semantic model to a file.\nWhich file format should you use?",
      "options": [
        {
          "letter": "A",
          "text": "PBIP",
          "mostVoted": true
        },
        {
          "letter": "B",
          "text": "PBIX",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "C",
          "text": "PBIT",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "D",
          "text": "PBIDS",
          "mostVoted": false
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "**PBIP — Power BI Project.** Saving as a project writes the report and the semantic model out as **plain-text folders on disk** instead of one binary file, which is what makes the model definition editable in VS Code and diffable in Git. The semantic model folder is where the **TMDL** files live (`definition/tables/*.tmdl`), so the TMDL extension for VS Code can open and bulk-edit them.\n\n- **B PBIX** – the standard Power BI Desktop file. It is a single binary archive; external text tooling cannot edit the model inside it.\n- **C PBIT** – a Power BI *template*: a PBIX without the data. Still binary, still not text-editable.\n- **D PBIDS** – a tiny \"data source\" connection file used to start a new report against a given source. It contains no model at all."
    },
