  {
    "id": "T1Q28",
    "type": "mcq",
    "stem": "You have a Fabric tenant that contains a warehouse. The warehouse uses row-level security (RLS).\nYou create a Direct Lake semantic model that uses the Delta tables and RLS of the warehouse.\nWhen users interact with a report built from the model, which mode will be used by the DAX queries?\nThis model uses Direct Lake on the SQL analytics endpoint, DirectLakeBehavior=Automatic, and the querying identity is subject to the SQL RLS policy.",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "DirectQuery"
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Dual"
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Direct Lake"
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Import"
      }
    ],
    "semanticVisuals": [],
    "caseStudy": null,
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q28",
    "sourceId": "T1Q28",
    "gradingEnabled": true,
    "scientificStatus": "APPROVED_CORRECTED",
    "r10Status": "CORRECTION_PROPOSED",
    "reviewNote": "Explicitly distinguishes SQL-endpoint Direct Lake from OneLake mode.",
    "remaining": "",
    "explanation": "A: SQL-endpoint RLS is a DirectQuery fallback case for this explicitly named Direct Lake variant with fallback enabled. Dual is a storage-mode setting, not the required fallback. Import is not introduced. Direct Lake on OneLake has different security/fallback behavior and must not be inferred from this scenario.",
    "answer": "A",
    "officialAnswer": "A",
    "original": {
      "type": "mcq",
      "officialAnswer": "A",
      "answer": "A",
      "stem": "You have a Fabric tenant that contains a warehouse. The warehouse uses row-level security (RLS).\nYou create a Direct Lake semantic model that uses the Delta tables and RLS of the warehouse.\nWhen users interact with a report built from the model, which mode will be used by the DAX queries?",
      "options": [
        {
          "letter": "A",
          "text": "DirectQuery",
          "mostVoted": true
        },
        {
          "letter": "B",
          "text": "Dual",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "C",
          "text": "Direct Lake",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "D",
          "text": "Import",
          "mostVoted": false
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "Direct Lake normally reads Delta/Parquet straight from OneLake with no SQL engine in the path. **Row-level security defined on the warehouse is enforced by the SQL engine**, so a model that must honour warehouse RLS cannot use that shortcut — it has to route the query through SQL. The doc says so in one sentence: *\"Power BI queries on a warehouse in Direct Lake mode will fall back to DirectQuery mode to abide by row-level security.\"*\n\nSo the DAX queries run in **DirectQuery** mode — **A**.\n\n- **C Direct Lake** – what the model is *configured* as, but not what the queries end up *using* once RLS forces the fallback. This is the trap, and 43% of the community falls into it.\n- **B Dual** – a storage mode you set on a table in a composite model. Direct Lake fallback does not produce it.\n- **D Import** – nothing is cached into the model; the data stays in the warehouse."
    },
    "sourceVisualReferences": {
      "exhibits": [],
      "answerImages": [],
      "optionImages": []
    },
    "visualResolution": "no_exhibit_needed",
    "refs": [
      {
        "title": "Microsoft documentation",
        "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/fundamentals/direct-lake-overview"
      }
    ],
    "reviewKind": "documentation-approved derived practice"
  },
