    "semanticVisuals": [],
    "caseStudy": null,
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q33",
    "sourceId": "T1Q33",
    "gradingEnabled": false,
    "scientificStatus": "R10_APPROVAL_CANDIDATE_NOT_REVALIDATED",
    "r10Status": "APPROVED",
    "reviewNote": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "An *implicit* measure is what Power BI creates on the fly when a report author drags a raw numeric column into a visual and lets it be summarised. You suppress that behaviour with the model-level property **`DiscourageImplicitMeasures`**, which forces authors to use explicit measures instead.\n\n- **A — Power BI Desktop.** Exposed in **Model Explorer** as the semantic model property *Discourage implicit measures* (it is also set automatically the moment you create a calculation group).\n- **B — Tabular Editor.** Sets `Model.DiscourageImplicitMeasures` directly against the TOM, which was the only way to do it before Desktop surfaced it.\n\nRejected:\n- **C SSMS** – can connect to the XMLA endpoint and script a model, but it is not a model-authoring tool for this property.\n- **D DAX Studio** – a query and performance-analysis tool. It is **read-only** against the model; it cannot change model metadata.",
    "answer": "AB",
    "officialAnswer": "AB",
    "original": {
      "type": "multi",
      "officialAnswer": "AB",
      "answer": "AB",
      "stem": "You have a Fabric tenant that contains a semantic model.\nYou need to prevent report creators from populating visuals by using implicit measures.\nWhat are two tools that you can use to achieve the goal? Each correct answer presents a complete solution.\nNOTE: Each correct answer is worth one point.",
      "options": [
        {
          "letter": "A",
          "text": "Microsoft Power BI Desktop",
          "mostVoted": true
        },
        {
          "letter": "B",
          "text": "Tabular Editor",
          "mostVoted": true
        },
        {
          "letter": "C",
          "text": "Microsoft SQL Server Management Studio (SSMS)",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "D",
          "text": "DAX Studio",
          "mostVoted": false
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "An *implicit* measure is what Power BI creates on the fly when a report author drags a raw numeric column into a visual and lets it be summarised. You suppress that behaviour with the model-level property **`DiscourageImplicitMeasures`**, which forces authors to use explicit measures instead.\n\n- **A — Power BI Desktop.** Exposed in **Model Explorer** as the semantic model property *Discourage implicit measures* (it is also set automatically the moment you create a calculation group).\n- **B — Tabular Editor.** Sets `Model.DiscourageImplicitMeasures` directly against the TOM, which was the only way to do it before Desktop surfaced it.\n\nRejected:\n- **C SSMS** – can connect to the XMLA endpoint and script a model, but it is not a model-authoring tool for this property.\n- **D DAX Studio** – a query and performance-analysis tool. It is **read-only** against the model; it cannot change model metadata."
    },
