    "r10Status": "APPROVED",
    "reviewNote": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "**Load to Tables** is the Lakehouse explorer command that converts files into managed Delta tables, and the doc states the output format outright: you can *\"load **CSV** or **Parquet** data and keep output in **Delta format with V-order optimization**.\"* Both halves of the requirement — delta format *and* V-Order — are covered by the one action, with no configuration.\n\n- **B / C — create a shortcut.** A shortcut is a *pointer*. It converts nothing; the underlying files stay CSV, which means a Tables-section shortcut would not even be recognised as a table.\n- **D — Optimize.** `OPTIMIZE` compacts small files in an **existing Delta table** (and can apply V-Order while doing so). It cannot turn CSV files into a Delta table in the first place, so there is nothing for it to act on yet.\n\nIn Lakehouse explorer: right-click the folder (here `Subfolder1`) → **Load to Tables** → *New table*.",
    "answer": "A",
    "officialAnswer": "A",
    "original": {
      "type": "mcq",
      "officialAnswer": "A",
      "answer": "A",
      "stem": "You have a Fabric tenant that contains a lakehouse named Lakehouse1. Lakehouse1 contains a subfolder named Subfolder1 that contains CSV\nfiles.\nYou need to convert the CSV files into the delta format that has V-Order optimization enabled.\nWhat should you do from Lakehouse explorer?",
      "options": [
        {
          "letter": "A",
          "text": "Use the Load to Tables feature.",
          "mostVoted": true
        },
        {
          "letter": "B",
          "text": "Create a new shortcut in the Files section.",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "C",
          "text": "Create a new shortcut in the Tables section.",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "D",
          "text": "Use the Optimize feature.",
          "mostVoted": false
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "**Load to Tables** is the Lakehouse explorer command that converts files into managed Delta tables, and the doc states the output format outright: you can *\"load **CSV** or **Parquet** data and keep output in **Delta format with V-order optimization**.\"* Both halves of the requirement — delta format *and* V-Order — are covered by the one action, with no configuration.\n\n- **B / C — create a shortcut.** A shortcut is a *pointer*. It converts nothing; the underlying files stay CSV, which means a Tables-section shortcut would not even be recognised as a table.\n- **D — Optimize.** `OPTIMIZE` compacts small files in an **existing Delta table** (and can apply V-Order while doing so). It cannot turn CSV files into a Delta table in the first place, so there is nothing for it to act on yet.\n\nIn Lakehouse explorer: right-click the folder (here `Subfolder1`) → **Load to Tables** → *New table*."
    },
