    "id": "T1Q43",
    "type": "mcq",
    "stem": "You have a Fabric tenant that contains a data pipeline.\nYou need to ensure that the pipeline runs every four hours on Mondays and Fridays.\nTo what should you set Repeat for the schedule?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Daily"
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "By the minute"
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Weekly"
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Hourly"
      }
    ],
    "semanticVisuals": [],
    "caseStudy": null,
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q43",
    "sourceId": "T1Q43",
    "gradingEnabled": false,
    "scientificStatus": "CORRECTION_PROPOSED",
    "r10Status": "AMBIGUOUS",
    "reviewNote": "Made active hours finite and avoided the inherited twelve-runs/week requirement.",
    "remaining": "Complete current primary-doc section review, source screenshot/case checks and native fixture where material; then independently challenge every final option.",
    "explanation": "A Fabric schedule has a single **Repeat** granularity, and only **Weekly** lets you pick *which days of the week* the schedule applies to. Set Repeat = **Weekly**, tick **Monday** and **Friday**, then add the six times (00:00, 04:00, 08:00, 12:00, 16:00, 20:00) to get the every-four-hours behaviour on just those two days.\n\n- **A Daily** – would run on all seven days. There is no day-of-week selector.\n- **D Hourly** – gives an every-N-hours interval, but applies it every day; it cannot be restricted to Monday and Friday.\n- **B By the minute** – same problem, at a finer interval.\n\nThe day-of-week restriction is the binding constraint, and Weekly is the only option that offers it.",
    "answer": "C",
    "officialAnswer": "C",
    "original": {
      "type": "mcq",
      "officialAnswer": "C",
      "answer": "C",
      "stem": "You have a Fabric tenant that contains a data pipeline.\nYou need to ensure that the pipeline runs every four hours on Mondays and Fridays.\nTo what should you set Repeat for the schedule?",
      "options": [
        {
          "letter": "A",
          "text": "Daily",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "B",
          "text": "By the minute",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "C",
          "text": "Weekly",
          "mostVoted": true
        },
        {
          "letter": "D",
          "text": "Hourly",
          "mostVoted": false
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "A Fabric schedule has a single **Repeat** granularity, and only **Weekly** lets you pick *which days of the week* the schedule applies to. Set Repeat = **Weekly**, tick **Monday** and **Friday**, then add the six times (00:00, 04:00, 08:00, 12:00, 16:00, 20:00) to get the every-four-hours behaviour on just those two days.\n\n- **A Daily** – would run on all seven days. There is no day-of-week selector.\n- **D Hourly** – gives an every-N-hours interval, but applies it every day; it cannot be restricted to Monday and Friday.\n- **B By the minute** – same problem, at a finer interval.\n\nThe day-of-week restriction is the binding constraint, and Weekly is the only option that offers it."
    },
