  {
    "id": "T1Q46",
    "type": "mcq",
    "stem": "You have a Fabric tenant that contains a warehouse.\nA user discovers that a report that usually takes two minutes to render has been running for 45 minutes and has still not rendered.\nYou need to identify what is preventing the report query from completing.\nWhich dynamic management view (DMV) should you use?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "sys.dm_exec_requests"
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "sys.dm_exec_sessions"
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "sys.dm_exec_connections"
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "sys.dm_pdw_exec_requests"
      }
    ],
    "semanticVisuals": [],
    "caseStudy": null,
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q46",
    "sourceId": "T1Q46",
    "gradingEnabled": false,
    "scientificStatus": "R10_APPROVAL_CANDIDATE_NOT_REVALIDATED",
    "r10Status": "APPROVED",
    "reviewNote": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "**`sys.dm_exec_requests`** lists every request **currently executing**, with the columns you need to diagnose a stuck query: `status`, `command`, `total_elapsed_time`, and — critically — **`blocking_session_id`** and **`wait_type` / `wait_time`**. Those last ones answer \"what is *preventing* the query from completing\".\n\nFabric Warehouse supports a small set of DMVs for exactly this task; the monitoring doc's worked example joins `sys.dm_exec_sessions`, `sys.dm_exec_requests` and `sys.dm_exec_connections`, and it is `dm_exec_requests` that carries the execution state.\n\n- **B `sys.dm_exec_sessions`** – who is connected (login, host, session state). It does not describe the running request.\n- **C `sys.dm_exec_connections`** – the transport layer: protocol, client address, connect time.\n- **D `sys.dm_pdw_exec_requests`** – the **Azure Synapse dedicated SQL pool (PDW)** equivalent. It is not one of the three DMVs Fabric Warehouse supports.",
    "answer": "A",
    "officialAnswer": "A",
    "original": {
      "type": "mcq",
      "officialAnswer": "A",
      "answer": "A",
      "stem": "You have a Fabric tenant that contains a warehouse.\nA user discovers that a report that usually takes two minutes to render has been running for 45 minutes and has still not rendered.\nYou need to identify what is preventing the report query from completing.\nWhich dynamic management view (DMV) should you use?",
      "options": [
        {
          "letter": "A",
          "text": "sys.dm_exec_requests",
          "mostVoted": true
        },
        {
          "letter": "B",
          "text": "sys.dm_exec_sessions",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "C",
          "text": "sys.dm_exec_connections",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "D",
          "text": "sys.dm_pdw_exec_requests",
          "mostVoted": false
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "**`sys.dm_exec_requests`** lists every request **currently executing**, with the columns you need to diagnose a stuck query: `status`, `command`, `total_elapsed_time`, and — critically — **`blocking_session_id`** and **`wait_type` / `wait_time`**. Those last ones answer \"what is *preventing* the query from completing\".\n\nFabric Warehouse supports a small set of DMVs for exactly this task; the monitoring doc's worked example joins `sys.dm_exec_sessions`, `sys.dm_exec_requests` and `sys.dm_exec_connections`, and it is `dm_exec_requests` that carries the execution state.\n\n- **B `sys.dm_exec_sessions`** – who is connected (login, host, session state). It does not describe the running request.\n- **C `sys.dm_exec_connections`** – the transport layer: protocol, client address, connect time.\n- **D `sys.dm_pdw_exec_requests`** – the **Azure Synapse dedicated SQL pool (PDW)** equivalent. It is not one of the three DMVs Fabric Warehouse supports."
    },
