    "id": "T1Q50",
    "type": "hotspot-dropdown",
    "stem": "You have a Fabric workspace named Workspace1 and an Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2 account named storage1. Workspace1 contains a\nlakehouse named Lakehouse1.\nYou need to create a shortcut to storage1 in Lakehouse1.\nWhich connection and endpoint should you specify? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.",
    "blanks": [
      {
        "label": "Connection:",
        "options": [
          "abfs",
          "abfss",
          "https"
        ],
        "answer": "https"
      },
      {
        "label": "Endpoint:",
        "options": [
          "blob",
          "dfs",
          "file"
        ],
        "answer": "dfs"
      }
    ],
    "semanticVisuals": [],
    "caseStudy": null,
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q50",
    "sourceId": "T1Q50",
    "gradingEnabled": false,
    "scientificStatus": "R10_APPROVAL_CANDIDATE_NOT_REVALIDATED",
    "r10Status": "APPROVED",
    "reviewNote": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "**https — dfs.** The ADLS Gen2 shortcut dialog asks for a **connection URL**, and the doc gives its exact shape:\n\n```\nhttps://<account_name>.dfs.core.windows.net\n```\n\n- **Connection = `https`.** The shortcut is created over the storage account's **HTTPS REST endpoint**. `abfs` / `abfss` are the **Hadoop driver** schemes you use from Spark code to *read* a path — they are not what you type when creating the shortcut.\n- **Endpoint = `dfs`.** ADLS Gen2 exposes two endpoints on the same account: `blob.core.windows.net` (flat Blob API) and `dfs.core.windows.net` (**Data Lake Storage Gen2 API**, with real hierarchical namespace support). Shortcuts require the **DFS** endpoint; `file` is Azure Files, a different service entirely.\n\nOnce the shortcut exists you address it inside Fabric with an `abfss://` OneLake path — which is what the `abfs`/`abfss` distractors are fishing for. One commenter who sat the exam reports the live item labels the first blank **\"protocol\"** rather than \"connection\"; the answer is the same.",
    "answer": null,
    "officialAnswer": "",
    "original": {
      "type": "hotspot-dropdown",
      "officialAnswer": "",
      "blanks": [
        {
          "label": "Connection:",
          "options": [
            "abfs",
            "abfss",
            "https"
          ],
          "answer": "https"
        },
        {
          "label": "Endpoint:",
          "options": [
            "blob",
            "dfs",
            "file"
          ],
          "answer": "dfs"
        }
      ],
      "stem": "You have a Fabric workspace named Workspace1 and an Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2 account named storage1. Workspace1 contains a\nlakehouse named Lakehouse1.\nYou need to create a shortcut to storage1 in Lakehouse1.\nWhich connection and endpoint should you specify? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.",
      "explanation": "**https — dfs.** The ADLS Gen2 shortcut dialog asks for a **connection URL**, and the doc gives its exact shape:\n\n```\nhttps://<account_name>.dfs.core.windows.net\n```\n\n- **Connection = `https`.** The shortcut is created over the storage account's **HTTPS REST endpoint**. `abfs` / `abfss` are the **Hadoop driver** schemes you use from Spark code to *read* a path — they are not what you type when creating the shortcut.\n- **Endpoint = `dfs`.** ADLS Gen2 exposes two endpoints on the same account: `blob.core.windows.net` (flat Blob API) and `dfs.core.windows.net` (**Data Lake Storage Gen2 API**, with real hierarchical namespace support). Shortcuts require the **DFS** endpoint; `file` is Azure Files, a different service entirely.\n\nOnce the shortcut exists you address it inside Fabric with an `abfss://` OneLake path — which is what the `abfs`/`abfss` distractors are fishing for. One commenter who sat the exam reports the live item labels the first blank **\"protocol\"** rather than \"connection\"; the answer is the same."
    },
