    "explanation": "**Automatic — Direct Lake.**\n\nThe exhibit is Performance analyzer over the model from Microsoft's *Analyze query processing for Direct Lake semantic models* article, which contains both a **table** and a **view**.\n\n**Blank 1 — Automatic.** `DirectLakeBehavior` has three settings:\n\n| Setting | Effect |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Automatic** (default) | use Direct Lake when possible, **fall back to DirectQuery** when not |\n| DirectLakeOnly | Direct Lake only; any query that cannot use it **fails** |\n| DirectQueryOnly | always DirectQuery |\n\nThe trace shows *both* modes in use — one visual served by Direct Lake, another falling back to DirectQuery because it reads a **view** (views always fall back; Direct Lake reads Delta tables). Mixed behaviour in one report is only possible under **Automatic**: `DirectLakeOnly` would have errored, `DirectQueryOnly` would have used DirectQuery throughout.\n\n**Blank 2 — Direct Lake.** The table visual is bound to the Delta **table**, so its columns are paged straight from OneLake with no SQL query — the Performance analyzer row shows a **Direct query** duration of 0 for it, which is the signature of Direct Lake. \"The composite model\" is not a query mode at all.",
