    "caseStudy": null,
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q53",
    "sourceId": "T1Q53",
    "gradingEnabled": false,
    "scientificStatus": "BLOCKED_RUNTIME",
    "r10Status": "CORRECTION_PROPOSED",
    "reviewNote": "Corrected undeclared tpepPickupDateTime identifier and table-name typo.",
    "remaining": "Inspect schema/code screenshots and run target Spark boundary/timezone fixture; current API docs not independently read.",
    "explanation": "The completed code:\n\n```python\ndf = spark.read.format(\"delta\").load(\"Tables/nyctaxi_raw\")\ndf2 = df.withColumn(\"pickupDate\", df['tpepPickupDateTime'].cast('date')) \\\n        .filter(\"fareAmount > 0 AND fareAmount < 100\")\n```\n\n**Blank 1 — `df.withColumn`.** The requirement is to **add** a column named `pickupDate`. `withColumn(colName, col)` *\"returns a new DataFrame by adding a column or replacing the existing column that has the same name\"* — and its two-argument shape matches the code.\n- `df.select` projects columns; it would drop everything not listed.\n- `df.withColumnsRenamed` **renames** existing columns (and takes a dict), which loses `tpepPickupDateTime`.\n- `df.columns` is a property returning a list of names, not a function.\n\n**Blank 2 — `.cast('date')`.** Only the **date portion** is wanted, so the timestamp is cast to Spark's `DateType`, which truncates the time. `.cast('pickupDate')` is not a type. `.alias('date')` only labels the column — it would leave the full timestamp value, and the name is already set by `withColumn`. `.getfield('date')` reads a subfield of a struct.\n\n**Blank 3 — `.filter(\"fareAmount > 0 AND fareAmount < 100\")`.** `filter` accepts a SQL expression string, and this one states exactly \"positive and less than 100\".\n- `.contains(\"1..100\")` is substring matching on text — wrong on every count.\n- `.when(...)` is a **column** function used inside `select`/`withColumn`; it is not a DataFrame method and cannot filter rows.\n- `.isin([1,100])` matches the two literal values 1 and 100, not the range between them.",
    "answer": null,
    "officialAnswer": "",
    "original": {
