    "explanation": "**No.** `df.explain()` prints the **query plan** — the parsed, analyzed, optimized logical plans and the physical plan Spark intends to run. It is a debugging and tuning tool. It computes no statistics at all, so it returns no min, max, mean or standard deviation.\n\nThe solution that meets the goal is **`df.summary()`** (see T1Q56), which returns count, mean, stddev, min, the quartiles and max, and covers string columns as well as numeric ones. `df.describe()` is the narrower sibling.\n\nAcross this set of four:\n\n| Question | Expression | Meets the goal? |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **T1Q54** | `df.explain()` | **No** — prints the query plan |\n| T1Q55 | `df.show()` | No — prints the first 20 rows |\n| **T1Q56** | `df.summary()` | **Yes** |\n| — | `df.describe()` | Yes (the other documented answer) |",
