    "reviewNote": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "**Yes.** `DESCRIBE HISTORY` returns the Delta table's **transaction log as a table** — one row per commit, with `version`, `timestamp`, `userName`, and crucially **`operation`** and `operationParameters`.\n\nMaintenance commands are ordinary Delta commits, so they appear there by name: `OPTIMIZE`, `VACUUM START` / `VACUUM END`, alongside `WRITE`, `MERGE` and the rest. Reading the `operation` column tells you directly whether maintenance has been run and when — exactly the goal.\n\n```sql\nDESCRIBE HISTORY customer\n```\n\nThe default history retention is 30 days, so this answers \"was maintenance performed recently\". Compare the other solutions in this set: `REFRESH TABLE` (T1Q58) only reloads cached metadata, and `EXPLAIN TABLE` (T1Q59) is not even valid syntax.",
    "answer": "A",
    "officialAnswer": "A",
