        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The requirement is *\"a dedicated, on-demand capacity that has **per-minute billing**\"*, and only one SKU family in the list is a Fabric capacity at all:\n\n| SKU | What it is | Billing |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **F** | **Fabric capacity** | **pay-as-you-go, billed per minute; pause and resume on demand** |\n| P | Power BI Premium capacity | monthly/yearly commitment, cannot be paused |\n| EM | Power BI Embedded (A-series successor for embedding) | monthly commitment |\n| A | Power BI Embedded, Azure-billed hourly | Power BI workloads only |\n\nAll Fabric capacities are **F** SKUs (F2 … F2048), they are purchased in Azure, and they can be paused so you pay only for the minutes you use — which is exactly \"on-demand … per-minute billing\". P and EM are Power BI–only and commitment-based; A SKUs are Power BI Embedded and do not carry the Fabric workloads the Research division needs."
    },
