    "reviewNote": "Added missing ABFS scheme with explicit lakehouse namespace assumption. Full case re-read also contradicts original CSV reader and direct-storage retrieval route.",
    "remaining": "Additional source/case defect found: Contoso Productline1 is Delta and must be retrieved through Lakehouse1/ResearchProduct shortcut. Candidate changed source format to Delta but direct source URI still does not fulfill the required retrieval route. Resolve shortcut target/table path and auth; do not execute as a compliant solution.",
    "explanation": "**delta — Tables/productline1.** The data preparation requirement is *\"All the Research division data in the lakehouses must be presented as **managed tables** in Lakehouse explorer.\"*\n\n**Format — `delta`.** A lakehouse managed table is a **Delta** table. Writing `csv` or `parquet` leaves you with files, which Lakehouse explorer shows under *Files*, not as a table.\n\n**Path — `Tables/productline1`.** The code uses **`.save(path)`**, not `.saveAsTable(name)`, so you must give the full relative path. Anything written directly under **`Tables/`** is auto-discovered and appears as a managed table.\n- `productline1` alone resolves outside the `Tables` area and errors (one commenter reports testing exactly this).\n- `Tables/research/productline1` adds an intermediate folder. A one-level-deep folder under `Tables` is treated as a **schema** container, not a table — the table would not surface where the requirement wants it.\n\n*(Had the code used `.saveAsTable(\"productline1\")` the bare name would have been correct — that is the distinction the distractors are testing.)*",
