    "sourceId": "T1Q66",
    "gradingEnabled": false,
    "scientificStatus": "CORRECTION_PROPOSED",
    "r10Status": "CORRECTION_PROPOSED",
    "reviewNote": "Restricted task to external metadata editor instead of denying Desktop capability.",
    "remaining": "Verify Tabular Editor official support/version and current XMLA permissions before approving the revised tool-selection item.",
    "explanation": "A **calculation group** is a tabular-model object (a calculation group table with calculation items). At the time this question was written, no first-party Microsoft surface could author one — you needed an external tool writing over the **XMLA endpoint**, and **Tabular Editor** is the tool Microsoft's own documentation and practice assessments name.\n\n- **C DAX Studio** – queries and profiles a model; it cannot modify model metadata.\n- **B the Power BI service** – no calculation-group authoring in the web modelling experience.\n\n**⚠ Doc drift.** **Power BI Desktop has since gained calculation group authoring** (Model view → *Calculation groups*, shipped in 2024), so on a current build **A is also a valid way to do it**. That is why the vote is only 55% D with 32% on A, and why several commenters say they would now answer A. The exam key is **D**; if you meet this item in the wild, note that the distinguishing detail is which version of Desktop is assumed.",
    "answer": "D",
    "officialAnswer": "D",
    "original": {
      "type": "mcq",
      "officialAnswer": "D",
      "answer": "D",
      "stem": "What should you use to implement calculation groups for the Research division semantic models?",
      "options": [
        {
          "letter": "A",
          "text": "Microsoft Power BI Desktop",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "B",
          "text": "the Power BI service",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "C",
          "text": "DAX Studio",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "D",
          "text": "Tabular Editor",
          "mostVoted": true
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "A **calculation group** is a tabular-model object (a calculation group table with calculation items). At the time this question was written, no first-party Microsoft surface could author one — you needed an external tool writing over the **XMLA endpoint**, and **Tabular Editor** is the tool Microsoft's own documentation and practice assessments name.\n\n- **C DAX Studio** – queries and profiles a model; it cannot modify model metadata.\n- **B the Power BI service** – no calculation-group authoring in the web modelling experience.\n\n**⚠ Doc drift.** **Power BI Desktop has since gained calculation group authoring** (Model view → *Calculation groups*, shipped in 2024), so on a current build **A is also a valid way to do it**. That is why the vote is only 55% D with 32% on A, and why several commenters say they would now answer A. The exam key is **D**; if you meet this item in the wild, note that the distinguishing detail is which version of Desktop is assumed."
    },
