      ],
      "stem": "You have a Fabric tenant.\nYou need to configure OneLake security for users shown in the following table.\nThe solution must follow the principle of least privilege.\nWhich permission should you assign to each user? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.",
      "explanation": "**ReadAll — ReadData.** These are the three lakehouse sharing permissions, and the doc maps each to an access path:\n\n| Permission | Grants |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Read** | open the lakehouse item — metadata only, no data |\n| **ReadAll** | *\"read all data using **Apache Spark** and OneLake APIs\"* |\n| **ReadData** | *\"read data from the **SQL analytics endpoint** through T-SQL\"*, subject to any SQL security policy |\n\n- **User1** needs *\"Read all the Spark data\"* → **ReadAll**.\n- **User2** needs *\"Read all the SQL endpoint data\"* → **ReadData**.\n\nPlain **Read** is insufficient for either: it lets you see the item but returns no data. And the two are not interchangeable — ReadData does not grant OneLake file access, and ReadAll is broader than the SQL endpoint, so swapping them would break least privilege as well as the requirement."
