    "id": "T1Q74",
    "type": "hotspot-dropdown",
    "stem": "You have a Fabric tenant that contains lakehouse named Lakehouse1. Lakehouse1 contains a Delta table with eight columns.\nYou receive new data that contains the same eight columns and two additional columns.\nYou create a Spark DataFrame and assign the DataFrame to a variable named df. The DataFrame contains the new data.\nYou need to add the new data to the Delta table to meet the following requirements:\n• Keep all the existing rows.\n• Ensure that all the new data is added to the table.\nHow should you complete the code? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.",
    "blanks": [
      {
        "label": "df.write.format(\"delta\").mode  ______",
        "options": [
          "(\"append\")",
          "(\"error\")",
          "(\"errorifexists\")",
          "(\"ignore\")",
          "(\"overwrite\")"
        ],
        "answer": "(\"append\")"
      },
      {
        "label": ".option  ______",
        "options": [
          "(\"mergeSchema\",\"false\")",
          "(\"mergeSchema\",\"true\")",
          "(\"overwriteSchema\",\"false\")",
          "(\"overwriteSchema\",\"true\")"
        ],
        "answer": "(\"mergeSchema\",\"true\")"
      }
    ],
    "semanticVisuals": [
      {
        "kind": "code",
        "title": "Original Delta schema evolution completion template",
        "language": "python",
        "content": "df.write.format(\"delta\").mode[Dropdown 1] \\\n    .option[Dropdown 2] \\\n    .saveAsTable(\"table\")"
      }
    ],
    "caseStudy": null,
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q74",
    "sourceId": "T1Q74",
    "gradingEnabled": false,
    "scientificStatus": "R10_APPROVAL_CANDIDATE_NOT_REVALIDATED",
    "r10Status": "APPROVED",
    "reviewNote": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "**`(\"append\")` — `(\"mergeSchema\",\"true\")`.** Each requirement maps to one blank.\n\n```python\ndf.write.format(\"delta\").mode(\"append\") \\\n  .option(\"mergeSchema\", \"true\") \\\n  .saveAsTable(\"table\")\n```\n\n**Blank 1 — *\"Keep all the existing rows\"* → `append`.** `overwrite` would replace them. `error` / `errorifexists` throw if the table exists; `ignore` silently does nothing — so with those, the new data would never land.\n\n**Blank 2 — *\"Ensure that all the new data is added\"* → `mergeSchema = true`.** The incoming DataFrame has **two columns the table does not have**. By default Delta enforces the schema and the write fails. Schema evolution fixes it: *\"Columns that are present in the DataFrame but missing from the table are automatically added as part of a write transaction when `write` … [has] `.option(\"mergeSchema\", \"true\")`.\"* The two new columns are added and existing rows get `NULL` for them.\n- `mergeSchema = false` is the default and would error.\n- `overwriteSchema` is for *replacing* a schema — changing a column's type or name, or dropping a column — and it only applies with `overwrite` mode, which would destroy the existing rows.",
    "answer": null,
    "officialAnswer": "",
    "original": {
      "type": "hotspot-dropdown",
      "officialAnswer": "",
      "blanks": [
        {
          "label": "df.write.format(\"delta\").mode  ______",
          "options": [
            "(\"append\")",
            "(\"error\")",
            "(\"errorifexists\")",
            "(\"ignore\")",
            "(\"overwrite\")"
          ],
          "answer": "(\"append\")"
        },
        {
          "label": ".option  ______",
          "options": [
            "(\"mergeSchema\",\"false\")",
            "(\"mergeSchema\",\"true\")",
            "(\"overwriteSchema\",\"false\")",
            "(\"overwriteSchema\",\"true\")"
          ],
          "answer": "(\"mergeSchema\",\"true\")"
        }
      ],
      "stem": "You have a Fabric tenant that contains lakehouse named Lakehouse1. Lakehouse1 contains a Delta table with eight columns.\nYou receive new data that contains the same eight columns and two additional columns.\nYou create a Spark DataFrame and assign the DataFrame to a variable named df. The DataFrame contains the new data.\nYou need to add the new data to the Delta table to meet the following requirements:\n• Keep all the existing rows.\n• Ensure that all the new data is added to the table.\nHow should you complete the code? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.",
      "explanation": "**`(\"append\")` — `(\"mergeSchema\",\"true\")`.** Each requirement maps to one blank.\n\n```python\ndf.write.format(\"delta\").mode(\"append\") \\\n  .option(\"mergeSchema\", \"true\") \\\n  .saveAsTable(\"table\")\n```\n\n**Blank 1 — *\"Keep all the existing rows\"* → `append`.** `overwrite` would replace them. `error` / `errorifexists` throw if the table exists; `ignore` silently does nothing — so with those, the new data would never land.\n\n**Blank 2 — *\"Ensure that all the new data is added\"* → `mergeSchema = true`.** The incoming DataFrame has **two columns the table does not have**. By default Delta enforces the schema and the write fails. Schema evolution fixes it: *\"Columns that are present in the DataFrame but missing from the table are automatically added as part of a write transaction when `write` … [has] `.option(\"mergeSchema\", \"true\")`.\"* The two new columns are added and existing rows get `NULL` for them.\n- `mergeSchema = false` is the default and would error.\n- `overwriteSchema` is for *replacing* a schema — changing a column's type or name, or dropping a column — and it only applies with `overwrite` mode, which would destroy the existing rows."
    },
