    "explanation": "**Full outer** is the only join kind that returns *\"all the rows in both tables\"* — matched rows once, plus unmatched rows from the left with nulls on the right, plus unmatched rows from the right with nulls on the left.\n\nThe visual query merge dialog offers the same set Power Query does:\n\n| Join kind | Returns |\n| --- | --- |\n| Inner | only rows that match in both |\n| Left outer | all from the left, matches from the right |\n| Right outer | all from the right, matches from the left |\n| **Full outer** | **all rows from both** |\n| Left anti | only left rows with no match |\n| Right anti | only right rows with no match |",
