    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "**Customers → Type 2, Products → Type 1.** The change action named in the requirements table *is* the definition of the SCD type:\n\n| Type | Behaviour on change |\n| --- | --- |\n| Type 0 | ignore the change — the attribute is fixed forever |\n| **Type 1** | **overwrite the existing value; no history kept** |\n| **Type 2** | **insert a new row (a new version), and close off the old one** |\n| Type 3 | keep a \"previous value\" column alongside the current one — one step of history, not a new row |\n\n- **Customers — \"Create a new version of the row\"** → **Type 2**. New rows, typically with a surrogate key plus effective start/end dates or an *is-current* flag, so the full history is queryable.\n- **Products — \"Overwrite the existing value in the latest row\"** → **Type 1**. *\"A Type 1 SCD always reflects the latest values, and when changes in source data are detected, the dimension table data is overwritten.\"*\n\nType 0 and Type 3 are distractors: neither matches a stated action.",
    "answer": null,
    "officialAnswer": "",
