  {
    "id": "T1Q79",
    "type": "mcq",
    "stem": "You have a Fabric workspace named Workspace1 and an Azure SQL database.\nYou plan to create a dataflow that will read data from the database, and then transform the data by performing an inner join.\nYou need to ignore spaces in the values when performing the inner join. The solution must minimize development effort.\nWhat should you do?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Append the queries by using fuzzy matching."
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Merge the queries by using fuzzy matching."
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Append the queries by using a lookup table."
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Merge the queries by using a lookup table."
      }
    ],
    "semanticVisuals": [],
    "caseStudy": null,
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q79",
    "sourceId": "T1Q79",
    "gradingEnabled": false,
    "scientificStatus": "R10_APPROVAL_CANDIDATE_NOT_REVALIDATED",
    "r10Status": "APPROVED",
    "reviewNote": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "Two independent decisions:\n\n**Merge, not Append.** *\"Merge queries … creates a new query from two queries in a **join**\"*; *\"Append queries … creates a new query that contains all rows from a first query **followed by** all rows from a second query\"* — a union. The requirement says **inner join**, so it is Merge.\n\n**Fuzzy matching, not a lookup table.** The join keys differ only by spaces, so exact matching would drop rows. Power Query's **fuzzy matching** option on the merge dialog *\"relies on … similarity\"* rather than exact equality and is *\"applied at the time of the merge operation\"*. Its **Ignore space** transformation option does exactly what is asked, and it is a checkbox — which is what satisfies *\"minimize development effort\"*.\n\nA lookup/transformation table is a manual mapping you have to build and maintain for every variation — far more effort. (It *is* an option within the fuzzy merge dialog, but it is not needed when a built-in option covers the case.)",
    "answer": "B",
    "officialAnswer": "B",
    "original": {
      "type": "mcq",
      "officialAnswer": "B",
      "answer": "B",
      "stem": "You have a Fabric workspace named Workspace1 and an Azure SQL database.\nYou plan to create a dataflow that will read data from the database, and then transform the data by performing an inner join.\nYou need to ignore spaces in the values when performing the inner join. The solution must minimize development effort.\nWhat should you do?",
      "options": [
        {
          "letter": "A",
          "text": "Append the queries by using fuzzy matching.",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "B",
          "text": "Merge the queries by using fuzzy matching.",
          "mostVoted": true
        },
        {
          "letter": "C",
          "text": "Append the queries by using a lookup table.",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "D",
          "text": "Merge the queries by using a lookup table.",
          "mostVoted": false
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "Two independent decisions:\n\n**Merge, not Append.** *\"Merge queries … creates a new query from two queries in a **join**\"*; *\"Append queries … creates a new query that contains all rows from a first query **followed by** all rows from a second query\"* — a union. The requirement says **inner join**, so it is Merge.\n\n**Fuzzy matching, not a lookup table.** The join keys differ only by spaces, so exact matching would drop rows. Power Query's **fuzzy matching** option on the merge dialog *\"relies on … similarity\"* rather than exact equality and is *\"applied at the time of the merge operation\"*. Its **Ignore space** transformation option does exactly what is asked, and it is a checkbox — which is what satisfies *\"minimize development effort\"*.\n\nA lookup/transformation table is a manual mapping you have to build and maintain for every variation — far more effort. (It *is* an option within the fuzzy merge dialog, but it is not needed when a built-in option covers the case.)"
    },
