  {
    "id": "T1Q81",
    "type": "mcq",
    "stem": "In the current Fabric lifecycle, a new lakehouse is created after automatic default semantic model creation was retired. You want to prevent new lakehouse tables from silently appearing in a semantic model. Which statement describes the current behavior?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "There is no automatic default-model creation/table synchronization to disable; explicitly select tables in a managed semantic model."
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Turn off query caching to stop automatic table additions."
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Remove workspace discovery endorsement to stop table synchronization."
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Disable RLS to stop semantic model table additions."
      }
    ],
    "semanticVisuals": [],
    "caseStudy": null,
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q81",
    "sourceId": "T1Q81",
    "gradingEnabled": true,
    "scientificStatus": "APPROVED_CORRECTED",
    "r10Status": "CORRECTION_PROPOSED",
    "reviewNote": "Replaced a retired setting task with an explicit current lifecycle question.",
    "remaining": "",
    "explanation": "A reflects the retired default-model lifecycle. Query caching controls caching, endorsement controls discovery, and RLS controls row visibility; none is a semantic schema synchronization switch. This is a revised lifecycle practice item, not an assertion that the historic source question is valid unchanged.",
    "answer": "A",
    "officialAnswer": "A",
    "original": {
      "type": "mcq",
      "officialAnswer": "A",
      "answer": "A",
      "stem": "You have a Fabric tenant that contains a lakehouse named Lakehouse1.\nYou need to prevent new tables added to Lakehouse1 from being added automatically to the default semantic model of the lakehouse.\nWhat should you configure?",
      "options": [
        {
          "letter": "A",
          "text": "the SQL analytics endpoint settings",
          "mostVoted": true
        },
        {
          "letter": "B",
          "text": "the semantic model settings",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "C",
          "text": "the workspace settings",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "D",
          "text": "the Lakehouse1 settings",
          "mostVoted": false
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The auto-add behaviour belongs to the **SQL analytics endpoint**, not to the lakehouse item and not to the semantic model. The setting is *\"Sync the default Power BI semantic model\"*, and the doc says where it lives: *\"To change this setting, open the settings of either the **SQL analytics endpoint** object of a lakehouse or the warehouse object.\"* Turning it off stops new tables and views being pushed into the default semantic model.\n\n- **B the semantic model settings** – the default semantic model is generated *for* you; it has no switch governing what the endpoint syncs into it. (40% of the community picks this.)\n- **D the Lakehouse1 settings** – covers the lakehouse item itself, not the endpoint.\n- **C the workspace settings** – no such per-workspace toggle.\n\nIn the UI: open the lakehouse, switch the view selector to **SQL analytics endpoint**, then **Settings → Default Power BI semantic model** and clear the sync option.\n\n*Note:* one commenter observes that Microsoft later changed the **default** so tables are *not* auto-added. That changes the default, not where the setting lives — **A** stands."
    },
    "sourceVisualReferences": {
      "exhibits": [],
      "answerImages": [],
      "optionImages": []
    },
    "visualResolution": "no_exhibit_needed",
    "refs": [
