  {
    "id": "T1Q82",
    "type": "hotspot-dropdown",
    "stem": "You have a Fabric tenant that contains a workspace named Workspace1. Workspace1 contains a lakehouse named Lakehouse1 and a warehouse\nnamed Warehouse1.\nYou need to create a new table in Warehouse1 named POSCustomers by querying the customer table in Lakehouse1.\nHow should you complete the T-SQL statement? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.",
    "blanks": [
      {
        "label": "Line 1",
        "options": [
          "CREATE TABLE dbo.POSCustomers",
          "CREATE TABLE dbo.POSCustomers AS CLONE OF",
          "CREATE TABLE dbo.POSCustomers AS SELECT"
        ],
        "answer": "CREATE TABLE dbo.POSCustomers AS SELECT"
      },
      {
        "label": "Final line",
        "options": [
          "FROM dbo.Customer",
          "FROM dbo.POSCustomers",
          "FROM lakehouse1.dbo.customer"
        ],
        "answer": "FROM lakehouse1.dbo.customer"
      }
    ],
    "semanticVisuals": [
      {
        "kind": "code",
        "title": "Original CREATE TABLE AS SELECT template",
        "language": "sql",
        "content": "[Dropdown 1]\n    DISTINCT customerid,\n    customer,\n    postalcode,\n    category\n[Dropdown 2];"
      }
    ],
    "caseStudy": null,
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q82",
    "sourceId": "T1Q82",
    "gradingEnabled": false,
    "scientificStatus": "R10_APPROVAL_CANDIDATE_NOT_REVALIDATED",
    "r10Status": "APPROVED",
    "reviewNote": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "**`CREATE TABLE dbo.POSCustomers AS SELECT` — `FROM lakehouse1.dbo.customer`.**\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE dbo.POSCustomers AS SELECT\n  DISTINCT customerid,\n           customer,\n           postalcode,\n           category\nFROM lakehouse1.dbo.customer;\n```\n\n**Blank 1 — CTAS.** The body is a `SELECT DISTINCT …` list, so the statement has to be **`CREATE TABLE … AS SELECT`**.\n- Plain `CREATE TABLE dbo.POSCustomers` expects a column definition list in parentheses, not a `SELECT`.\n- **`AS CLONE OF` cannot be used here** for two reasons: cloning takes a table reference, not a `SELECT DISTINCT` projection; and the doc states *\"Table clones **across warehouses** in a workspace are not currently supported\"* — and a lakehouse is a different item again.\n\n**Blank 2 — three-part name across items.** Within one workspace, a warehouse can read a lakehouse's SQL analytics endpoint by **cross-database query** using `item.schema.table`, hence `lakehouse1.dbo.customer`. `dbo.Customer` would look inside Warehouse1, where the table does not exist, and `dbo.POSCustomers` is the table being created.",
    "answer": null,
    "officialAnswer": "",
    "original": {
      "type": "hotspot-dropdown",
      "officialAnswer": "",
      "blanks": [
        {
          "label": "Line 1",
          "options": [
