  {
    "id": "T1Q86",
    "type": "mcq",
    "stem": "You have a Fabric tenant.\nYou plan to create a data pipeline named Pipeline1. Pipeline1 will include two activities that will execute in sequence.\nYou need to ensure that a failure of the first activity will NOT block the second activity.\nWhich conditional path should you configure between the first activity and the second activity?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Upon Failure"
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Upon Completion"
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Upon Skip"
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Upon Skip"
      }
    ],
    "semanticVisuals": [],
    "caseStudy": null,
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q86",
    "sourceId": "T1Q86",
    "gradingEnabled": false,
    "scientificStatus": "R10_APPROVAL_CANDIDATE_NOT_REVALIDATED",
    "r10Status": "APPROVED_WITH_NONBLOCKING_EDITS",
    "reviewNote": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "Pipeline activities are wired together with **conditional paths**, and each one is a different promise about when the next activity runs:\n\n| Path | Runs the next activity when the first… |\n| --- | --- |\n| On success | succeeded |\n| On fail | failed |\n| On skip | was skipped |\n| **On completion** | **finished — success *or* failure** |\n\nThe requirement is that *\"a failure of the first activity will NOT block the second activity\"* — the second must run either way. That is **Upon Completion**.\n\n- **A Upon Failure** inverts the problem: the second activity would run *only* if the first failed, and would be skipped when it succeeded.\n- **C / D Upon Skip** (listed twice — a typo in the question) fires only when the first activity was itself skipped, which is not the case here.",
    "answer": "B",
    "officialAnswer": "B",
    "original": {
      "type": "mcq",
      "officialAnswer": "B",
      "answer": "B",
      "stem": "You have a Fabric tenant.\nYou plan to create a data pipeline named Pipeline1. Pipeline1 will include two activities that will execute in sequence.\nYou need to ensure that a failure of the first activity will NOT block the second activity.\nWhich conditional path should you configure between the first activity and the second activity?",
      "options": [
        {
          "letter": "A",
          "text": "Upon Failure",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "B",
          "text": "Upon Completion",
          "mostVoted": true
        },
        {
          "letter": "C",
          "text": "Upon Skip",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "D",
          "text": "Upon Skip",
          "mostVoted": false
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "Pipeline activities are wired together with **conditional paths**, and each one is a different promise about when the next activity runs:\n\n| Path | Runs the next activity when the first… |\n| --- | --- |\n| On success | succeeded |\n| On fail | failed |\n| On skip | was skipped |\n| **On completion** | **finished — success *or* failure** |\n\nThe requirement is that *\"a failure of the first activity will NOT block the second activity\"* — the second must run either way. That is **Upon Completion**.\n\n- **A Upon Failure** inverts the problem: the second activity would run *only* if the first failed, and would be skipped when it succeeded.\n- **C / D Upon Skip** (listed twice — a typo in the question) fires only when the first activity was itself skipped, which is not the case here."
    },
    "sourceVisualReferences": {
