    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q87",
    "sourceId": "T1Q87",
    "gradingEnabled": false,
    "scientificStatus": "CORRECTION_PROPOSED",
    "r10Status": "AMBIGUOUS",
    "reviewNote": "Made the required automated rule an explicit prerequisite.",
    "remaining": "Complete current primary-doc section review, source screenshot/case checks and native fixture where material; then independently challenge every final option.",
    "explanation": "**Best Practice Analyzer (BPA) in Tabular Editor** scans the whole model against a rule set and lists every object that violates a rule. Microsoft's published BPA rules for Power BI include exactly this one — *\"Set `IsAvailableInMdx` to false / set Summarize By to None on non-attribute columns\"* — and BPA rules can match on naming patterns such as columns ending in `Key`. One click, a complete list. That is what *\"minimize effort\"* rewards.\n\n- **C Model view** – you would click each column in turn and read its Properties pane. Correct but manual across every table.\n- **B Model explorer** – a navigation tree over model objects. Still one column at a time, and no rule evaluation.\n- **A DAX Formatter in DAX Studio** – pretty-prints DAX expressions. It does not inspect column properties at all.",
    "answer": "D",
    "officialAnswer": "D",
    "original": {
      "type": "mcq",
      "officialAnswer": "D",
      "answer": "D",
      "stem": "You have a Microsoft Power BI semantic model.\nYou need to identify any surrogate key columns in the model that have the Summarize By property set to a value other than to None. The solution\nmust minimize effort.\nWhat should you use?",
      "options": [
        {
