    "id": "T1Q89",
    "type": "mcq",
    "stem": "You have a Fabric tenant that contains a semantic model. The model contains 15 tables.\nYou need to programmatically change each column that ends in the word Key to meet the following requirements:\n• Hide the column.\n• Set Nullable to False\n• Set Summarize By to None.\n• Set Available in MDX to False.\n• Mark the column as a key column.\nWhat should you use?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Microsoft Power BI Desktop"
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "ALM Toolkit"
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Tabular Editor"
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "DAX Studio"
      }
    ],
    "semanticVisuals": [],
    "caseStudy": null,
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q89",
    "sourceId": "T1Q89",
    "gradingEnabled": false,
    "scientificStatus": "R10_APPROVAL_CANDIDATE_NOT_REVALIDATED",
    "r10Status": "APPROVED",
    "reviewNote": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "The word doing the work is **programmatically**, across **15 tables**, driven by a naming convention. **Tabular Editor** has a **C# scripting** engine over the Tabular Object Model, so the whole job is a short loop:\n\n```csharp\nforeach (var c in Model.AllColumns.Where(c => c.Name.EndsWith(\"Key\"))) {\n    c.IsHidden        = true;\n    c.IsNullable     = false;\n    c.SummarizeBy     = AggregateFunction.None;\n    c.IsAvailableInMDX = false;\n    c.IsKey           = true;\n}\n```\n\nThose five lines are the five bullet points in the question, one for one.\n\n- **A Power BI Desktop** – every property is there in the Properties pane, but you would set them by hand, column by column, across 15 tables. Not programmatic.\n- **B ALM Toolkit** – *compares and deploys* differences between two models. It does not author property changes.\n- **D DAX Studio** – queries and profiles a model; it is read-only against model metadata.",
    "answer": "C",
    "officialAnswer": "C",
    "original": {
      "type": "mcq",
      "officialAnswer": "C",
      "answer": "C",
      "stem": "You have a Fabric tenant that contains a semantic model. The model contains 15 tables.\nYou need to programmatically change each column that ends in the word Key to meet the following requirements:\n• Hide the column.\n• Set Nullable to False\n• Set Summarize By to None.\n• Set Available in MDX to False.\n• Mark the column as a key column.\nWhat should you use?",
      "options": [
        {
          "letter": "A",
          "text": "Microsoft Power BI Desktop",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "B",
