  {
    "id": "T1Q90",
    "type": "hotspot-dropdown",
    "stem": "You have a Microsoft Power BI semantic model.\nYou plan to implement calculation groups.\nYou need to create a calculation item that will change the context from the selected date to month-to-date (MTD).\nHow should you complete the DAX expression? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.",
    "blanks": [
      {
        "label": "______  (",
        "options": [
          "CALCULATE",
          "GENERATE",
          "MEASURE"
        ],
        "answer": "CALCULATE"
      },
      {
        "label": "______  (),   DATESMTD ( 'Date'[Date] )",
        "options": [
          "COMBINEVALUES",
          "SELECTEDMEASURE",
          "SELECTEDVALUE"
        ],
        "answer": "SELECTEDMEASURE"
      }
    ],
    "semanticVisuals": [
      {
        "kind": "code",
        "title": "Original month-to-date calculation item template",
        "language": "dax",
        "content": "[Dropdown 1] (\n    [Dropdown 2] (),\n    DATESMTD ( 'Date'[Date] )\n)"
      }
    ],
    "caseStudy": null,
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q90",
    "sourceId": "T1Q90",
    "gradingEnabled": false,
    "scientificStatus": "R10_APPROVAL_CANDIDATE_NOT_REVALIDATED",
    "r10Status": "APPROVED",
    "reviewNote": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "**CALCULATE — SELECTEDMEASURE.** The finished calculation item is the standard MTD pattern:\n\n```dax\nCALCULATE (\n    SELECTEDMEASURE (),\n    DATESMTD ( 'Date'[Date] )\n)\n```\n\n**Blank 1 — `CALCULATE`.** Changing the filter context is what `CALCULATE` does: it evaluates its first argument under the filters given in the remaining arguments. Here that filter is `DATESMTD`, which returns the month-to-date set of dates.\n- `GENERATE` produces a cross-join style table; `MEASURE` is a DAX-query keyword for defining a measure, not an expression.\n\n**Blank 2 — `SELECTEDMEASURE()`.** A calculation item must work with *whatever measure the user puts in the visual*. `SELECTEDMEASURE` is the placeholder for it: it *\"returns a reference to the measure that is currently in context when a calculation item is being evaluated\"*, and the engine substitutes the real measure at query time. Without it the item could only ever transform one hard-coded measure.\n- `SELECTEDVALUE` returns a scalar from a *column* when exactly one value is filtered — unrelated.\n- `COMBINEVALUES` concatenates values for relationship keys.",
    "answer": null,
    "officialAnswer": "",
    "original": {
      "type": "hotspot-dropdown",
      "officialAnswer": "",
      "blanks": [
        {
          "label": "______  (",
          "options": [
            "CALCULATE",
            "GENERATE",
            "MEASURE"
          ],
          "answer": "CALCULATE"
        },
        {
          "label": "______  (),   DATESMTD ( 'Date'[Date] )",
          "options": [
            "COMBINEVALUES",
            "SELECTEDMEASURE",
            "SELECTEDVALUE"
          ],
          "answer": "SELECTEDMEASURE"
        }
      ],
      "stem": "You have a Microsoft Power BI semantic model.\nYou plan to implement calculation groups.\nYou need to create a calculation item that will change the context from the selected date to month-to-date (MTD).\nHow should you complete the DAX expression? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.",
      "explanation": "**CALCULATE — SELECTEDMEASURE.** The finished calculation item is the standard MTD pattern:\n\n```dax\nCALCULATE (\n    SELECTEDMEASURE (),\n    DATESMTD ( 'Date'[Date] )\n)\n```\n\n**Blank 1 — `CALCULATE`.** Changing the filter context is what `CALCULATE` does: it evaluates its first argument under the filters given in the remaining arguments. Here that filter is `DATESMTD`, which returns the month-to-date set of dates.\n- `GENERATE` produces a cross-join style table; `MEASURE` is a DAX-query keyword for defining a measure, not an expression.\n\n**Blank 2 — `SELECTEDMEASURE()`.** A calculation item must work with *whatever measure the user puts in the visual*. `SELECTEDMEASURE` is the placeholder for it: it *\"returns a reference to the measure that is currently in context when a calculation item is being evaluated\"*, and the engine substitutes the real measure at query time. Without it the item could only ever transform one hard-coded measure.\n- `SELECTEDVALUE` returns a scalar from a *column* when exactly one value is filtered — unrelated.\n- `COMBINEVALUES` concatenates values for relationship keys."
    },
