  {
    "id": "T1Q92",
    "type": "mcq",
    "stem": "You have a custom Direct Lake semantic model named Model1 that has one billion rows of data.\nYou use Tabular Editor to connect to Model1 by using the XMLA endpoint.\nYou need to ensure that when users interact with reports based on Model1, their queries always use Direct Lake mode.\nWhat should you do?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "From Model, configure the Default Mode option."
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "From Partitions, configure the Mode option."
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "From Model, configure the Storage Location option."
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "From Model, configure the Direct Lake Behavior option."
      }
    ],
    "semanticVisuals": [],
    "caseStudy": null,
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q92",
    "sourceId": "T1Q92",
    "gradingEnabled": false,
    "scientificStatus": "R10_APPROVAL_CANDIDATE_NOT_REVALIDATED",
    "r10Status": "APPROVED_WITH_NONBLOCKING_EDITS",
    "reviewNote": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "A Direct Lake model can silently **fall back to DirectQuery** when data cannot be loaded efficiently into memory (guardrail exceeded, a view rather than a table, RLS on the warehouse, and so on). The switch that governs this is the model-level **`DirectLakeBehavior`** property, exposed in Tabular Editor as **Direct Lake Behavior** on the Model node:\n\n| Value | Effect |\n| --- | --- |\n| `Automatic` (default) | Direct Lake, falling back to DirectQuery when needed |\n| **`DirectLakeOnly`** | **Direct Lake only — a query that cannot use it fails instead of falling back** |\n| `DirectQueryOnly` | always DirectQuery |\n\nTo guarantee that *\"their queries always use Direct Lake mode\"*, set it to **Direct Lake only**.\n\n- **B Partitions → Mode** – a Direct Lake table has a single `DirectLake` partition; this does not control fallback.\n- **A Model → Default Mode** – sets the storage mode for *new* tables, not the fallback policy.\n- **C Model → Storage Location** – where the model data sits. Unrelated.",
    "answer": "D",
    "officialAnswer": "D",
    "original": {
      "type": "mcq",
      "officialAnswer": "D",
      "answer": "D",
      "stem": "You have a custom Direct Lake semantic model named Model1 that has one billion rows of data.\nYou use Tabular Editor to connect to Model1 by using the XMLA endpoint.\nYou need to ensure that when users interact with reports based on Model1, their queries always use Direct Lake mode.\nWhat should you do?",
      "options": [
        {
          "letter": "A",
          "text": "From Model, configure the Default Mode option.",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "B",
          "text": "From Partitions, configure the Mode option.",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "C",
          "text": "From Model, configure the Storage Location option.",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "D",
          "text": "From Model, configure the Direct Lake Behavior option.",
          "mostVoted": true
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "A Direct Lake model can silently **fall back to DirectQuery** when data cannot be loaded efficiently into memory (guardrail exceeded, a view rather than a table, RLS on the warehouse, and so on). The switch that governs this is the model-level **`DirectLakeBehavior`** property, exposed in Tabular Editor as **Direct Lake Behavior** on the Model node:\n\n| Value | Effect |\n| --- | --- |\n| `Automatic` (default) | Direct Lake, falling back to DirectQuery when needed |\n| **`DirectLakeOnly`** | **Direct Lake only — a query that cannot use it fails instead of falling back** |\n| `DirectQueryOnly` | always DirectQuery |\n\nTo guarantee that *\"their queries always use Direct Lake mode\"*, set it to **Direct Lake only**.\n\n- **B Partitions → Mode** – a Direct Lake table has a single `DirectLake` partition; this does not control fallback.\n- **A Model → Default Mode** – sets the storage mode for *new* tables, not the fallback policy.\n- **C Model → Storage Location** – where the model data sits. Unrelated."
    },
