    "explanation": "The exhibit shows, for each column: a **Valid / Error / Empty** bar with percentages, a **bar chart of the value distribution**, and a *\"n distinct, n unique\"* footer. Three separate Data-view checkboxes produce those three things:\n\n| Option | What it adds to the exhibit |\n| --- | --- |\n| **D — Show column quality details** | the **Valid / Error / Empty** percentages |\n| **A — Show column value distribution** | the **bar chart** plus the *distinct / unique* counts |\n| **C — Enable column profile** | the underlying profiling that feeds the *Column profile* pane |\n\n- **B — Enable details pane** is not one of the Data-view profiling options; nothing in the exhibit corresponds to it.\n\nAll three live on the **View** ribbon in Power Query, under *Data preview*. Note the counts are based on the **top 1,000 rows** unless you switch profiling to the entire data set (the same default that makes T1Q19 answerable).",
