    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "**Descriptive.** The work described is: read the data, then draw column charts showing the **distribution** of retained versus lost customers across geography, products purchased, age and tenure. That is summarising and presenting **what happened** — the definition of descriptive analytics.\n\n- **A diagnostic** – the trap, at 22% of the vote, because slicing by four attributes *feels* like investigating causes. But diagnostic analytics establishes **why**: drill-down into root cause, correlation analysis, hypothesis testing. Charting distributions does not attribute causation — it shows the shape of the data and leaves the *why* to the reader.\n- **D predictive** would score each customer with a churn probability (a trained model).\n- **C prescriptive** would recommend the retention action to take.\n\n*(Compare T1Q98, the same taxonomy tested with a simpler exhibit.)*",
    "answer": "B",
