    "explanation": "**Min and max** are **column statistics**, and those appear in the **details pane**, not on the column headers. Three checkboxes have to be on, and they stack:\n\n- **B — Enable column profile.** Turns on profiling. Without it there are no statistics to show.\n- **E — Enable details pane.** Opens the pane at the bottom of the Power Query window.\n- **C — Show column profile in details pane.** Routes the profile (Column statistics + Value distribution) *into* that pane, which is where **Min** and **Max** are listed.\n\nRejected:\n- **A Show column value distribution** – the little bar chart under the header. It shows the *shape* of the data, not min/max values.\n- **D Show column quality details** – Valid / Error / Empty percentages. Nothing about magnitude.\n\nNote the query returns **500 rows**, under the 1,000-row profiling default, so the statistics cover the whole result without switching to whole-dataset profiling.\n\n*(Contrast T1Q96, where the exhibit shows header-level quality bars and distribution charts, so the answer there is A, C and D.)*",
    "answer": "BCE",
