          "mostVoted": true
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "**`Table.Profile`** returns one row per column with exactly the statistics listed. The doc enumerates them: *\"minimum, maximum, average, standard deviation, count, null count, distinct count.\"* All five requested values — Count, Average, Null count, Distinct count and Standard deviation — are in that set.\n\n- **A `Table.Schema`** – returns *metadata*: column names, positions, data types, nullability. No statistics. (It is also spelled with a capital S.)\n- **B `Table.View`** – an advanced function for building a custom query folding handler. Nothing to do with profiling.\n- **C `Table.FuzzyGroup`** – groups rows by approximate similarity of a key.\n\n*(Same function as T1Q14, asked from the statistics side rather than the maximum-value side.)*"
