    "explanation": "**delta — Tables/productline2.** Identical reasoning to T1Q65, applied to Productline2 (whose source in `storage2` is CSV rather than delta — which is why the read uses `format('csv')` either way).\n\nThe data preparation requirement is *\"All the Research division data in the lakehouses must be presented as **managed tables** in Lakehouse explorer.\"*\n\n- **`delta`** — a managed lakehouse table is a Delta table. `csv` or `parquet` would leave files under *Files*.\n- **`Tables/productline2`** — the code calls **`.save(path)`**, so it needs the full relative path, and anything written directly under `Tables/` is auto-discovered as a managed table. A bare `productline2` resolves outside the Tables area and errors; `Tables/research/productline2` puts a schema folder in between, so the table would not appear where the requirement wants it.",
