      ],
      "stem": "You have a Fabric workspace that uses the default Spark starter pool and runtime version 1.2.\nYou plan to read a CSV file named Sales_raw.csv in a lakehouse, select columns, and save the data as a Delta table to the managed area of the\nlakehouse. Sales_raw.csv contains 12 columns.\nYou have the following code.\nFor each of the following statements, select Yes if the statement is true. Otherwise, select No.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.",
      "explanation": "**No — No — Yes.**\n\n**1. Reads only the four selected columns → No.** *(The PDF answer-key image marks **Yes** here; it is wrong.)* Column pruning at the storage layer is a property of **columnar** formats — Parquet and Delta keep each column in its own chunk, so unread columns are never fetched. **CSV is row-based**: every line must be read and scanned for delimiters before any field can be located. The `.select(...)` runs on the rows Spark has already read, so the full file is read either way.\n\nThis also contradicts the answer key of **T1Q45**, which poses the *identical* statement over the *identical* code and marks it **No** — the reading that matches documented behaviour. The community agrees: the two top comments here (+41, +9) both answer No; a third (+12) answers Yes.\n\n**2. The Year column replaces the OrderDate column → No.** `withColumn(\"Year\", year(\"OrderDate\"))` *adds* a column. The doc: it *\"returns a new DataFrame by adding a column or replacing the existing column **that has the same name**\"* — the name here is `Year`, not `OrderDate`, so `OrderDate` survives untouched. (The table also ends up partitioned by `Year`, which does not remove `OrderDate` either.)\n\n**3. `inferSchema=\"true\"` increases execution time → Yes.** Inference costs an **extra pass over the file**: Spark reads it once to deduce column types, then again to load. Supplying an explicit schema skips that pass.\n\n*(Two OCR slips in the exhibit: `.red` is `.read`, `\"heade\"` is `\"header\"`.)*"
    },
    "sourceVisualReferences": {
      "exhibits": [
        "p287_i1.png",
        "p287_i2.png"
      ],
