    "stem": "Note: This question is part of a series of questions that present the same scenario. Each question in the series contains a unique solution that\nmight meet the stated goals. Some question sets might have more than one correct solution, while others might not have a correct solution.\nAfter you answer a question in this section, you will NOT be able to return to it. As a result, these questions will not appear in the review screen.\nYou have a Fabric tenant that contains a semantic model named Model1.\nYou discover that the following query performs slowly against Model1.\nYou need to reduce the execution time of the query.\nSolution: You replace line 4 by using the following code:\nNOT ( CALCULATE ( COUNTROWS ( 'Order Item' ) ) < 0)\nDoes this meet the goal?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Yes"
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "No"
      }
    ],
    "semanticVisuals": [
      {
        "kind": "code",
        "title": "Original slow DAX query (line 4)",
        "language": "dax",
        "content": "EVALUATE\nFILTER (\n    VALUES ( Customer[Customer Name] ),\n    CALCULATE ( COUNTROWS ( 'Order Item' ) ) > 0\n)\nORDER BY Customer[Customer Name]"
      }
    ],
    "caseStudy": null,
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q118",
    "sourceId": "T1Q118",
    "gradingEnabled": false,
    "scientificStatus": "R10_APPROVAL_CANDIDATE_NOT_REVALIDATED",
    "r10Status": "APPROVED",
    "reviewNote": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "**No.** The proposed line 4 is\n\n```dax\nNOT ( CALCULATE ( COUNTROWS ( 'Order Item' ) ) < 0 )\n```\n\n- **The result is wrong.** A row count is never negative, so `< 0` is always false and `NOT(false)` is always **true**. Every customer passes the filter, including those with no orders — which is precisely who the original `> 0` excluded.\n- **It is no faster.** `CALCULATE ( COUNTROWS ( ... ) )` is still evaluated for every customer; only the comparison around it changed. The cost of counting every related row is untouched.\n\nBoth halves fail. The working solution in this set is `NOT ISEMPTY ( CALCULATETABLE ( 'Order Item' ) )` (T1Q108), which changes the expensive part rather than the comparison.",
    "answer": "B",
    "officialAnswer": "B",
    "original": {
      "type": "yesno",
      "officialAnswer": "B",
      "answer": "B",
      "stem": "Note: This question is part of a series of questions that present the same scenario. Each question in the series contains a unique solution that\nmight meet the stated goals. Some question sets might have more than one correct solution, while others might not have a correct solution.\nAfter you answer a question in this section, you will NOT be able to return to it. As a result, these questions will not appear in the review screen.\nYou have a Fabric tenant that contains a semantic model named Model1.\nYou discover that the following query performs slowly against Model1.\nYou need to reduce the execution time of the query.\nSolution: You replace line 4 by using the following code:\nNOT ( CALCULATE ( COUNTROWS ( 'Order Item' ) ) < 0)\nDoes this meet the goal?",
      "options": [
        {
          "letter": "A",
          "text": "Yes",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "B",
          "text": "No",
          "mostVoted": true
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "**No.** The proposed line 4 is\n\n```dax\nNOT ( CALCULATE ( COUNTROWS ( 'Order Item' ) ) < 0 )\n```\n\n- **The result is wrong.** A row count is never negative, so `< 0` is always false and `NOT(false)` is always **true**. Every customer passes the filter, including those with no orders — which is precisely who the original `> 0` excluded.\n- **It is no faster.** `CALCULATE ( COUNTROWS ( ... ) )` is still evaluated for every customer; only the comparison around it changed. The cost of counting every related row is untouched.\n\nBoth halves fail. The working solution in this set is `NOT ISEMPTY ( CALCULATETABLE ( 'Order Item' ) )` (T1Q108), which changes the expensive part rather than the comparison."
    },
