      "explanation": "Third variant of the same Contoso question, with yet another option set. Here the path-based read is offered with the **correct** path, so it wins:\n\n```python\ndf = spark.read.format(\"delta\").load(\"Tables/ResearchProduct\")\n```\n\nThis is the form Microsoft documents for reading a shortcut from Spark: `spark.read.format(\"delta\").load(\"Tables/MyShortcut\")`.\n\n- **B** – `Files/ResearchProduct` is the wrong area. The data preparation requirement says the data must be *\"presented as managed tables in Lakehouse explorer\"*, which puts the shortcut under **`Tables/`**.\n- **C / D** – `external_table(...)` is not a Fabric notebook construct (and C is missing a closing quote).\n\n| Question | Correct option | Why |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| T1Q4 | `spark.sql(\"SELECT * FROM Lakehouse1.ResearchProduct\")` | the only path option given was `Tables/productline1/…` — wrong path |\n| T1Q111 | `spark.sql(\"SELECT * FROM Lakehouse1.ResearchProduct\")` | the only path option given was `Files/…` — wrong area |\n| **T1Q119** | **`spark.read…load(\"Tables/ResearchProduct\")`** | **the correct path is finally on offer** |"
