    "id": "T1Q121",
    "type": "hotspot-dropdown",
    "stem": "You have a Fabric tenant that contains a warehouse named WH1.\nYou have source data in a CSV file that has the following fields:\n• SalesTransactionID\n• SaleDate\n• CustomerCode\n• CustomerName\n• CustomerAddress\n• ProductCode\n• ProductName\n• Quantity\n• UnitPrice\nYou plan to implement a star schema for the tables in WH1. The dimension tables in WH1 will implement Type 2 slowly changing dimension (SCD)\nlogic.\nYou need to design the tables that will be used for sales transaction analysis and load the source data.\nWhich type of target table should you specify for the CustomerName, CustomerCode, and SaleDate fields? To answer, select the appropriate\noptions in the answer area.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.",
    "blanks": [
      {
        "label": "CustomerCode:",
        "options": [
          "Dimension",
          "Fact",
          "Factless fact",
          "Junk dimension"
        ],
        "answer": "Dimension"
      },
      {
        "label": "CustomerName:",
        "options": [
          "Dimension",
          "Fact",
          "Factless fact",
          "Junk dimension"
        ],
        "answer": "Dimension"
      },
      {
        "label": "SaleDate:",
        "options": [
          "Dimension",
          "Fact",
          "Factless fact",
          "Junk dimension"
        ],
        "answer": "Fact"
      }
    ],
    "semanticVisuals": [],
    "caseStudy": null,
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q121",
    "sourceId": "T1Q121",
    "gradingEnabled": false,
    "scientificStatus": "CORRECTION_PROPOSED",
    "r10Status": "AMBIGUOUS",
    "reviewNote": "Distinguished raw transaction date placement from Date dimension attributes.",
    "remaining": "Complete current primary-doc section review, source screenshot/case checks and native fixture where material; then independently challenge every final option.",
    "explanation": "**Dimension — Dimension — Fact.**\n\nThe star schema over this CSV is:\n\n- **FactSales** — one row per sales transaction: `SalesTransactionID` (a degenerate dimension), the date of the sale, the foreign keys to the customer and product dimensions, and the measures `Quantity` and `UnitPrice`.\n- **DimCustomer** (Type 2) — `CustomerCode` as the natural/business key, plus `CustomerName` and `CustomerAddress` as the attributes whose changes are versioned.\n- **DimProduct** (Type 2) — `ProductCode`, `ProductName`.\n\n**`CustomerCode` and `CustomerName` → Dimension.** Descriptive attributes of a customer, versioned by the Type 2 logic. They are not a *junk dimension* either — a junk dimension collects unrelated low-cardinality flags and indicators, not a business key and a name.\n\n**`SaleDate` → Fact.** *(The PDF answer-key image marks **Dimension**; it is wrong.)* `SaleDate` is **when the transaction happened** — an attribute of the *event*, so it belongs on the fact row (as the date itself, or as a `DateKey` pointing at a conformed date dimension). Two things rule out loading it into a dimension:\n1. **A date dimension is generated, not loaded from transactions.** It has to be contiguous — every day in the range, including days with no sales — so seeding it from the `SaleDate` values in a sales file would leave gaps. (T1Q62 makes exactly this point: *\"There is no existing data source for the date dimension\"*, so it must be generated.)\n2. **The question states the dimension tables implement Type 2 SCD logic.** A date dimension is never Type 2 — 17 March 2024 does not change and get a new version. Putting `SaleDate` in a Type 2 dimension is incoherent.\n\n**Factless fact** is the remaining distractor: that is a fact table with no measures (attendance, coverage). This one has `Quantity` and `UnitPrice`, so it is an ordinary fact table.\n\nThe community is unanimous against the key on this blank — the three comments that answer it (+20, +11, +4) all say **Dim, Dim, Fact**.",
    "answer": null,
    "officialAnswer": "",
    "original": {
      "type": "hotspot-dropdown",
      "officialAnswer": "",
      "blanks": [
        {
          "label": "CustomerCode:",
          "options": [
            "Dimension",
            "Fact",
