    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "**Lookup** — the activity that both *runs* a stored procedure and *returns* its result set to the rest of the pipeline: *\"Lookup activity reads and returns the content of a configuration file or table. It also returns the result of executing a query or stored procedure. The output can be a singleton value or an array of attributes, which can be consumed in a subsequent copy, transformation, or control flow activity.\"*\n\n- **A Get metadata** – returns *metadata about a file or folder* (name, size, last modified, child items). It cannot execute a stored procedure.\n- **B Copy data** – can call a stored procedure as a source, but it writes the rows to a sink instead of exposing them downstream.\n- **D Append variable** – appends a value to an array variable; it executes nothing.\n\n*(This question appears four times in the bank with different distractor sets — T1Q83, T1Q114, T1Q122, T1Q128. The answer is Lookup every time.)*",
