      "explanation": "Fourth variant of the Contoso shortcut-access question. Here, as in T1Q119, the **correct path** is on offer:\n\n```python\ndf = spark.read.format(\"delta\").load(\"Tables/ResearchProduct\")\n```\n\nThe case study creates `ResearchProduct` as a shortcut in `Lakehouse1`, the source data in `storage1` is already **delta**, and the data preparation requirement is that it be *\"presented as managed tables in Lakehouse explorer\"* — so it lives under **`Tables/`**.\n\n- **B** – `Tables/productline1/ResearchProduct` inserts the *workspace* name into the path. A lakehouse-relative table path does not include it (and a folder level under `Tables/` would be read as a schema).\n- **A** – `Lakehouse1.Tables.ResearchProduct` invents a three-part name; `Tables` is a storage area, not a SQL schema.\n- **C** – `external_table(...)` is not a Fabric notebook construct."
