        {
          "letter": "C",
          "text": "Enable Refresh for the default semantic model.",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "D",
          "text": "From the Endorsement and discovery settings of LH1, select Make discoverable.",
          "mostVoted": false
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doc gives two ways to get objects into the default semantic model, and the first is this setting: *\"Manually enable the **Sync the default Power BI semantic model** setting that will automatically add objects to the semantic model\"* (the alternative being to add tables manually).\n\n- **A Disable Query Caching** – affects whether query results are cached for report viewers. It adds nothing to the model.\n- **C Enable Refresh** – governs when *data* is reloaded, not which *objects* are in the model.\n- **D Make discoverable** – an endorsement/discovery setting that lets other users find the item in the OneLake data hub. Unrelated.\n\n*(This is the mirror image of T1Q81, which asks how to **stop** the auto-add. Same setting, opposite direction. Note that the setting is reached through the **SQL analytics endpoint** view of the lakehouse — the wording \"from the settings pane of LH1\" in this option is loose, but it is the only option that names the right control.)*"
    },
