    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "Split the columns by what each one *describes*:\n\n| Column | Describes | Goes to |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `TransactionID` | the transaction | FactSales (degenerate dimension) |\n| `Date` | when the transaction happened | FactSales |\n| **`ProductID`** | **a unique ID for each product** | **DimProduct** (key) |\n| **`ProductName`** | **a unique name for each product** | **DimProduct** (attribute) |\n| **`ProductColor`** | **a descriptive attribute of the product** | **DimProduct** (attribute) |\n| `SalesAmount` | the money for the transaction | FactSales (measure) |\n\nSo DimProduct = **ProductColor, ProductID, ProductName** — **A**. A dimension holds the *who / what* context; the fact table holds the numeric measures and the event keys.\n\n- **B** and **D** include `SalesAmount`, a **measure**. Measures belong in the fact table; putting one in a dimension would fix the amount per product rather than per transaction.\n- **C** includes `Date` and `TransactionID`, both attributes of the *transaction*, not of the product.",
    "answer": "A",
    "officialAnswer": "A",
