  {
    "id": "T1Q141",
    "type": "mcq",
    "stem": "You have a Fabric tenant that contains a workspace named Workspace1.\nYou plan to deploy a semantic model named Model1 by using the XMLA endpoint.\nYou need to optimize the deployment of Model1. The solution must minimize how long it takes to deploy Model1.\nWhat should you do in Workspace1?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Select Small semantic model storage format."
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Select Users can edit data models in the Power BI service."
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Set Enable Cache for Shortcuts to On."
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Select Large semantic model storage format."
      }
    ],
    "semanticVisuals": [],
    "caseStudy": null,
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q141",
    "sourceId": "T1Q141",
    "gradingEnabled": false,
    "scientificStatus": "R10_APPROVAL_CANDIDATE_NOT_REVALIDATED",
    "r10Status": "APPROVED_WITH_NONBLOCKING_EDITS",
    "reviewNote": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "**Large semantic model storage format.** Microsoft recommends it specifically for XMLA deployments, regardless of model size: *\"If you're planning to use XMLA endpoint-based tools for semantic model **write** operations, be sure to enable the setting, **even for semantic models that you wouldn't necessarily characterize as a large semantic model**. When enabled, the large semantic model storage format can **improve XMLA write operations performance**.\"*\n\nThe reason is how the model is persisted: the large format stores the model in **premium files** with incremental, per-object writes, instead of serialising the whole model on every write. Deployments touch far less data and finish faster.\n\n- **A Small semantic model storage format** – the opposite, and the default. Slower XMLA writes.\n- **B Users can edit data models in the Power BI service** – enables web modelling. Nothing to do with XMLA deployment speed.\n- **C Enable Cache for Shortcuts** – a OneLake shortcut caching setting for external data reads. Unrelated to semantic models.",
    "answer": "D",
    "officialAnswer": "D",
    "original": {
      "type": "mcq",
      "officialAnswer": "D",
      "answer": "D",
      "stem": "You have a Fabric tenant that contains a workspace named Workspace1.\nYou plan to deploy a semantic model named Model1 by using the XMLA endpoint.\nYou need to optimize the deployment of Model1. The solution must minimize how long it takes to deploy Model1.\nWhat should you do in Workspace1?",
      "options": [
        {
          "letter": "A",
          "text": "Select Small semantic model storage format.",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "B",
          "text": "Select Users can edit data models in the Power BI service.",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "C",
          "text": "Set Enable Cache for Shortcuts to On.",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "D",
          "text": "Select Large semantic model storage format.",
          "mostVoted": true
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "**Large semantic model storage format.** Microsoft recommends it specifically for XMLA deployments, regardless of model size: *\"If you're planning to use XMLA endpoint-based tools for semantic model **write** operations, be sure to enable the setting, **even for semantic models that you wouldn't necessarily characterize as a large semantic model**. When enabled, the large semantic model storage format can **improve XMLA write operations performance**.\"*\n\nThe reason is how the model is persisted: the large format stores the model in **premium files** with incremental, per-object writes, instead of serialising the whole model on every write. Deployments touch far less data and finish faster.\n\n- **A Small semantic model storage format** – the opposite, and the default. Slower XMLA writes.\n- **B Users can edit data models in the Power BI service** – enables web modelling. Nothing to do with XMLA deployment speed.\n- **C Enable Cache for Shortcuts** – a OneLake shortcut caching setting for external data reads. Unrelated to semantic models."
    },
