    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "**`cache.abf`.** In a Power BI project's `.SemanticModel` folder, `cache.abf` is the **Analysis Services backup file** holding the model's **cached data** — the actual imported rows from your data sources. It is binary, it can be very large, and it is the one file that would push real data values into the repository. `.gitignore` it.\n\nWhat the others are:\n- **D `model.bim`** – the model **definition** in TMSL/JSON: tables, columns, measures, relationships. Metadata only, and it is exactly what you *want* under version control.\n- **A `unappliedChanges.json`** – pending edits not yet applied to the model. Metadata.\n- **C `localSettings.json`** – per-user, per-machine settings. It *should* also be excluded — and the doc notes *\"By default, Git ignores this file\"* — but it holds preferences, not data values, so it does not answer the question as asked.\n\nThe default `.gitignore` that Power BI Desktop generates for a project already excludes `cache.abf` and `.pbi/localSettings.json` for these reasons.",
    "answer": "B",
    "officialAnswer": "B",
    "original": {
      "type": "mcq",
      "officialAnswer": "B",
      "answer": "B",
      "stem": "You have a Microsoft Power BI project that contains a semantic model.\nYou plan to use Azure DevOps for version control.\nYou need to modify the .gitignore file to prevent the data values from the data sources from being pushed to the repository.\nWhich file should you reference?",
      "options": [
        {
          "letter": "A",
          "text": "unappliedChanges.json",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "B",
          "text": "cache.abf",
          "mostVoted": true
        },
        {
          "letter": "C",
          "text": "localSettings.json",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "D",
          "text": "model.bim",
          "mostVoted": false
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "**`cache.abf`.** In a Power BI project's `.SemanticModel` folder, `cache.abf` is the **Analysis Services backup file** holding the model's **cached data** — the actual imported rows from your data sources. It is binary, it can be very large, and it is the one file that would push real data values into the repository. `.gitignore` it.\n\nWhat the others are:\n- **D `model.bim`** – the model **definition** in TMSL/JSON: tables, columns, measures, relationships. Metadata only, and it is exactly what you *want* under version control.\n- **A `unappliedChanges.json`** – pending edits not yet applied to the model. Metadata.\n- **C `localSettings.json`** – per-user, per-machine settings. It *should* also be excluded — and the doc notes *\"By default, Git ignores this file\"* — but it holds preferences, not data values, so it does not answer the question as asked.\n\nThe default `.gitignore` that Power BI Desktop generates for a project already excludes `cache.abf` and `.pbi/localSettings.json` for these reasons."
    },
