      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Enforce strict access control for all data connection types"
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Enable Cache for Shortcuts"
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "License mode"
      }
    ],
    "semanticVisuals": [],
    "caseStudy": null,
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q143",
    "sourceId": "T1Q143",
    "gradingEnabled": false,
    "scientificStatus": "R10_APPROVAL_CANDIDATE_NOT_REVALIDATED",
    "r10Status": "APPROVED",
    "reviewNote": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "**License mode.** The XMLA endpoint is not available on **Pro** workspaces at all. Microsoft scopes it explicitly: *\"Power BI Premium, Premium Per User, and Power BI Embedded workspaces use an XMLA endpoint…\"* — Pro is absent from that list. So the blocker is the workspace's licensing tier, and the fix is to change **Workspace settings → License mode** to Premium per user, Premium capacity, Embedded, or a Fabric capacity.\n\n- **A Users can edit data models in the Power BI service** – enables browser modelling; it does not expose an XMLA endpoint.\n- **B Enforce strict access control for all data connection types** – a data-connection governance setting.\n- **C Enable Cache for Shortcuts** – OneLake shortcut caching. Unrelated.\n\nOnly once the workspace is on a supported licence do the other XMLA switches (the tenant setting, and the capacity's Read Write endpoint setting) become relevant.",
    "answer": "D",
    "officialAnswer": "D",
    "original": {
      "type": "mcq",
      "officialAnswer": "D",
      "answer": "D",
      "stem": "You have a Fabric tenant that contains a workspace named Workspace1. Workspace1 uses Pro license mode and contains a semantic model\nnamed Model1.\nYou need to ensure that Model1 supports XMLA connections.\nWhich setting should modify?",
      "options": [
        {
          "letter": "A",
          "text": "Users can edit data models in the Power BI service",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "B",
          "text": "Enforce strict access control for all data connection types",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "C",
          "text": "Enable Cache for Shortcuts",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "D",
          "text": "License mode",
          "mostVoted": true
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "**License mode.** The XMLA endpoint is not available on **Pro** workspaces at all. Microsoft scopes it explicitly: *\"Power BI Premium, Premium Per User, and Power BI Embedded workspaces use an XMLA endpoint…\"* — Pro is absent from that list. So the blocker is the workspace's licensing tier, and the fix is to change **Workspace settings → License mode** to Premium per user, Premium capacity, Embedded, or a Fabric capacity.\n\n- **A Users can edit data models in the Power BI service** – enables browser modelling; it does not expose an XMLA endpoint.\n- **B Enforce strict access control for all data connection types** – a data-connection governance setting.\n- **C Enable Cache for Shortcuts** – OneLake shortcut caching. Unrelated.\n\nOnly once the workspace is on a supported licence do the other XMLA switches (the tenant setting, and the capacity's Read Write endpoint setting) become relevant."
    },
