    "id": "T1Q145",
    "type": "hotspot-dropdown",
    "stem": "You have a Fabric tenant that contains a lakehouse named LH1.\nYou need to deploy a new semantic model. The solution must meet the following requirements:\n• Support complex calculated columns that include aggregate functions, calculated tables, and Multidimensional Expressions (MDX) user\nhierarchies.\n• Minimize page rendering times.\nHow should you configure the model? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.",
    "blanks": [
      {
        "label": "Mode:",
        "options": [
          "Direct Lake",
          "DirectQuery",
          "Import"
        ],
        "answer": "Import"
      },
      {
        "label": "Query Caching:",
        "options": [
          "Capacity default",
          "Off",
          "On"
        ],
        "answer": "On"
      }
    ],
    "semanticVisuals": [],
    "caseStudy": null,
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q145",
    "sourceId": "T1Q145",
    "gradingEnabled": false,
    "scientificStatus": "R10_APPROVAL_CANDIDATE_NOT_REVALIDATED",
    "r10Status": "APPROVED_WITH_NONBLOCKING_EDITS",
    "reviewNote": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "**Import — On.**\n\n**Mode — Import.** The first requirement lists three things that **Direct Lake does not support**. From the storage-mode comparison table in the Direct Lake docs:\n\n| Capability | Direct Lake | Import | DirectQuery |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Calculated columns with aggregate functions | **No** | **Yes** | No |\n| Calculated tables | **No** | **Yes** | No |\n| MDX user hierarchies | **No** | **Yes** | Yes |\n\nOnly **Import** answers Yes to all three. (Direct Lake carves out a narrow exception for calculation groups, what-if parameters and field parameters, which implicitly create calculated tables — but not for the general case the requirement describes.) DirectQuery fails on calculated columns and calculated tables, and is the slowest of the three anyway.\n\n**Query Caching — On.** The second requirement is *\"minimize page rendering times\"*. Query caching stores the results of a report's queries so that subsequent loads are served from the cache instead of re-querying the model — it is the setting whose stated purpose is faster report loads. *Capacity default* leaves it to chance; *Off* forgoes the benefit. It is available on Premium/Embedded and applies to **Import** models, which fits the mode chosen above.",
    "answer": null,
    "officialAnswer": "",
    "original": {
      "type": "hotspot-dropdown",
      "officialAnswer": "",
      "blanks": [
        {
          "label": "Mode:",
          "options": [
            "Direct Lake",
            "DirectQuery",
            "Import"
          ],
          "answer": "Import"
        },
        {
          "label": "Query Caching:",
          "options": [
            "Capacity default",
            "Off",
            "On"
          ],
          "answer": "On"
        }
      ],
      "stem": "You have a Fabric tenant that contains a lakehouse named LH1.\nYou need to deploy a new semantic model. The solution must meet the following requirements:\n• Support complex calculated columns that include aggregate functions, calculated tables, and Multidimensional Expressions (MDX) user\nhierarchies.\n• Minimize page rendering times.\nHow should you configure the model? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.",
      "explanation": "**Import — On.**\n\n**Mode — Import.** The first requirement lists three things that **Direct Lake does not support**. From the storage-mode comparison table in the Direct Lake docs:\n\n| Capability | Direct Lake | Import | DirectQuery |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Calculated columns with aggregate functions | **No** | **Yes** | No |\n| Calculated tables | **No** | **Yes** | No |\n| MDX user hierarchies | **No** | **Yes** | Yes |\n\nOnly **Import** answers Yes to all three. (Direct Lake carves out a narrow exception for calculation groups, what-if parameters and field parameters, which implicitly create calculated tables — but not for the general case the requirement describes.) DirectQuery fails on calculated columns and calculated tables, and is the slowest of the three anyway.\n\n**Query Caching — On.** The second requirement is *\"minimize page rendering times\"*. Query caching stores the results of a report's queries so that subsequent loads are served from the cache instead of re-querying the model — it is the setting whose stated purpose is faster report loads. *Capacity default* leaves it to chance; *Off* forgoes the benefit. It is available on Premium/Embedded and applies to **Import** models, which fits the mode chosen above."
    },
