  {
    "id": "T1Q146",
    "type": "hotspot-yesno",
    "stem": "You have the following KQL query.\nFor each of the following statements, select Yes if the statement is true. Otherwise, select No.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.",
    "statements": [
      {
        "text": "The query excludes sales that have a Status of Cancelled.",
        "answer": "Yes"
      },
      {
        "text": "The query calculates the total sales of each product category for the last 30 days.",
        "answer": "Yes"
      },
      {
        "text": "The query includes product categories that have had zero sales during the last 30 days.",
        "answer": "No"
      }
    ],
    "semanticVisuals": [
      {
        "kind": "code",
        "title": "Original KQL aggregation and filtering query",
        "language": "kql",
        "content": "Sales\n| where Status != \"Cancelled\"\n| where OrderDate >= ago(30d)\n| summarize TotalSales = sum(SalesAmount) by ProductCategory\n| where TotalSales > 0"
      }
    ],
    "caseStudy": null,
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q146",
    "sourceId": "T1Q146",
    "gradingEnabled": false,
    "scientificStatus": "R10_APPROVAL_CANDIDATE_NOT_REVALIDATED",
    "r10Status": "APPROVED",
    "reviewNote": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "**Yes — Yes — No.** Read the KQL one operator at a time:\n\n```kusto\nSales\n| where Status != \"Cancelled\"                              // 1\n| where OrderDate >= ago(30d)                              // 2\n| summarize TotalSales = sum(SalesAmount) by ProductCategory   // 2\n| where TotalSales > 0                                     // 3\n```\n\n**1. Excludes cancelled sales → Yes.** `!=` is \"not equal to\", so `where Status != \"Cancelled\"` keeps every row whose status is anything other than Cancelled.\n\n**2. Total sales per product category for the last 30 days → Yes.** `ago(30d)` returns the timestamp 30 days before now, so `OrderDate >= ago(30d)` keeps the last 30 days. `summarize sum(SalesAmount) by ProductCategory` then totals within each category. Both halves of the statement hold.\n\n**3. Includes categories with zero sales → No.** Two independent reasons:\n- `summarize … by ProductCategory` only produces groups for categories that **have rows** in the filtered input. A category with no sales in the window contributes no rows, so no group.\n- The final `| where TotalSales > 0` explicitly discards anything that totalled zero (or less, e.g. a refund-only category).\n\n*(One commenter reads statement 2 as No; the last line filters *after* the summarize, so it does not change what is being calculated — it only trims the output. The answer key and the other comments give Yes/Yes/No.)*",
    "answer": null,
    "officialAnswer": "",
    "original": {
      "type": "hotspot-yesno",
      "officialAnswer": "",
      "statements": [
        {
          "text": "The query excludes sales that have a Status of Cancelled.",
          "answer": "Yes"
        },
        {
          "text": "The query calculates the total sales of each product category for the last 30 days.",
          "answer": "Yes"
        },
        {
          "text": "The query includes product categories that have had zero sales during the last 30 days.",
          "answer": "No"
        }
      ],
      "stem": "You have the following KQL query.\nFor each of the following statements, select Yes if the statement is true. Otherwise, select No.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.",
      "explanation": "**Yes — Yes — No.** Read the KQL one operator at a time:\n\n```kusto\nSales\n| where Status != \"Cancelled\"                              // 1\n| where OrderDate >= ago(30d)                              // 2\n| summarize TotalSales = sum(SalesAmount) by ProductCategory   // 2\n| where TotalSales > 0                                     // 3\n```\n\n**1. Excludes cancelled sales → Yes.** `!=` is \"not equal to\", so `where Status != \"Cancelled\"` keeps every row whose status is anything other than Cancelled.\n\n**2. Total sales per product category for the last 30 days → Yes.** `ago(30d)` returns the timestamp 30 days before now, so `OrderDate >= ago(30d)` keeps the last 30 days. `summarize sum(SalesAmount) by ProductCategory` then totals within each category. Both halves of the statement hold.\n\n**3. Includes categories with zero sales → No.** Two independent reasons:\n- `summarize … by ProductCategory` only produces groups for categories that **have rows** in the filtered input. A category with no sales in the window contributes no rows, so no group.\n- The final `| where TotalSales > 0` explicitly discards anything that totalled zero (or less, e.g. a refund-only category).\n\n*(One commenter reads statement 2 as No; the last line filters *after* the summarize, so it does not change what is being calculated — it only trims the output. The answer key and the other comments give Yes/Yes/No.)*"
    },
