    "id": "T1Q151",
    "type": "mcq",
    "stem": "You need to create a Microsoft Power BI file that will be used to create multiple reports. The solution must meet the following requirements:\n• The file must include predefined data source connections.\n• The file must include the report structure and formatting.\n• The file must NOT contain any data.\nWhich file format should you use?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "PBIT"
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "PBIDS"
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "PBIX"
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "PBIP"
      }
    ],
    "semanticVisuals": [],
    "caseStudy": null,
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q151",
    "sourceId": "T1Q151",
    "gradingEnabled": false,
    "scientificStatus": "R10_APPROVAL_CANDIDATE_NOT_REVALIDATED",
    "r10Status": "APPROVED",
    "reviewNote": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "**PBIT — a Power BI template.** Match the three requirements against what each format holds:\n\n| Format | Data source connections | Report structure & formatting | Contains data |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **PBIT** (template) | **yes** | **yes** | **no** |\n| PBIX (report) | yes | yes | **yes** |\n| PBIDS (data source) | yes | no | no |\n| PBIP (project) | yes | yes | yes — `cache.abf` holds the imported data |\n\nA `.pbit` is a `.pbix` with the data cache stripped out: queries, model, measures, visuals and theme all survive, and opening one prompts for parameter values and then refreshes. That is precisely a reusable starting point for *\"multiple reports\"* with no data in it.\n\n- **C PBIX** fails the \"no data\" requirement.\n- **B PBIDS** is only a connection definition — no report structure at all.\n- **D PBIP** is the folder-based project format for source control; it includes `cache.abf`, which is the data (see T1Q142).",
    "answer": "A",
    "officialAnswer": "A",
    "original": {
      "type": "mcq",
      "officialAnswer": "A",
      "answer": "A",
      "stem": "You need to create a Microsoft Power BI file that will be used to create multiple reports. The solution must meet the following requirements:\n• The file must include predefined data source connections.\n• The file must include the report structure and formatting.\n• The file must NOT contain any data.\nWhich file format should you use?",
      "options": [
        {
          "letter": "A",
          "text": "PBIT",
          "mostVoted": true
        },
        {
          "letter": "B",
          "text": "PBIDS",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "C",
          "text": "PBIX",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "D",
          "text": "PBIP",
          "mostVoted": false
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "**PBIT — a Power BI template.** Match the three requirements against what each format holds:\n\n| Format | Data source connections | Report structure & formatting | Contains data |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **PBIT** (template) | **yes** | **yes** | **no** |\n| PBIX (report) | yes | yes | **yes** |\n| PBIDS (data source) | yes | no | no |\n| PBIP (project) | yes | yes | yes — `cache.abf` holds the imported data |\n\nA `.pbit` is a `.pbix` with the data cache stripped out: queries, model, measures, visuals and theme all survive, and opening one prompts for parameter values and then refreshes. That is precisely a reusable starting point for *\"multiple reports\"* with no data in it.\n\n- **C PBIX** fails the \"no data\" requirement.\n- **B PBIDS** is only a connection definition — no report structure at all.\n- **D PBIP** is the folder-based project format for source control; it includes `cache.abf`, which is the data (see T1Q142)."
