  {
    "id": "T1Q154",
    "type": "mcq",
    "stem": "You have a Fabric tenant that contains a workspace named Workspace1. Workspace1 contains a data pipeline named Pipeline1 and a lakehouse\nnamed Lakehouse1.\nYou perform the following actions:\n• Create a workspace named Workspace2.\n• Create a deployment pipeline named DeployPipeline1 that will deploy items from Workspace1 to Workspace2.\n• Add a folder named Folder1 to Workspace1.\n• Move Lakehouse1 to Folder1.\n• Run DeployPipeline1.\nWhich structure will Workspace2 have when DeployPipeline1 is complete?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "\\Folder1\\Pipeline1 \\Folder1\\Lakehouse1"
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "\\Pipeline1 \\Lakehouse1"
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "\\Pipeline1 \\Folder1\\Lakehouse1"
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "\\Folder1\\Lakehouse1"
      }
    ],
    "semanticVisuals": [],
    "caseStudy": null,
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q154",
    "sourceId": "T1Q154",
    "gradingEnabled": false,
    "scientificStatus": "R10_APPROVAL_CANDIDATE_NOT_REVALIDATED",
    "r10Status": "APPROVED",
    "reviewNote": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "**`\\Pipeline1` and `\\Folder1\\Lakehouse1`.** Two rules combine.\n\n**1. Folders travel with their items.** The doc: *\"In Deployment pipelines, **folders are considered part of an item's name** (an item name includes its full path). When an item is deployed, after its path was changed (moved from folder A to folder B, for example), then Deployment pipelines applies this change to its paired item during deployment… **If folder B doesn't exist in the stage we're deploying to, it's created in its workspace first.**\"*\n\nLakehouse1 was moved into `Folder1` **before** the deployment ran, so its full name is now `Folder1\\Lakehouse1`. Workspace2 gets `Folder1` created for it, with Lakehouse1 inside.\n\n**2. Pipeline1 never moved.** It is still at the root of Workspace1, so it deploys to the root of Workspace2 — and it *does* deploy; Data pipelines are a supported item type.\n\nRejected:\n- **D `\\Folder1\\Lakehouse1`** only – drops Pipeline1 entirely. Nothing excluded it from the deployment.\n- **B `\\Pipeline1` `\\Lakehouse1`** – assumes folders are ignored by deployment. The doc says the opposite.\n- **A** – puts Pipeline1 in Folder1 too, but it was never moved there.\n\n*Note:* the vote is a three-way split (C 41 / D 39 / B 20), which is a good sign that the folder rule is worth memorising.",
    "answer": "C",
    "officialAnswer": "C",
    "original": {
      "type": "mcq",
      "officialAnswer": "C",
      "answer": "C",
      "stem": "You have a Fabric tenant that contains a workspace named Workspace1. Workspace1 contains a data pipeline named Pipeline1 and a lakehouse\nnamed Lakehouse1.\nYou perform the following actions:\n• Create a workspace named Workspace2.\n• Create a deployment pipeline named DeployPipeline1 that will deploy items from Workspace1 to Workspace2.\n• Add a folder named Folder1 to Workspace1.\n• Move Lakehouse1 to Folder1.\n• Run DeployPipeline1.\nWhich structure will Workspace2 have when DeployPipeline1 is complete?",
      "options": [
        {
          "letter": "A",
          "text": "\\Folder1\\Pipeline1 \\Folder1\\Lakehouse1",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "B",
          "text": "\\Pipeline1 \\Lakehouse1",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "C",
          "text": "\\Pipeline1 \\Folder1\\Lakehouse1",
          "mostVoted": true
        },
        {
          "letter": "D",
          "text": "\\Folder1\\Lakehouse1",
          "mostVoted": false
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "**`\\Pipeline1` and `\\Folder1\\Lakehouse1`.** Two rules combine.\n\n**1. Folders travel with their items.** The doc: *\"In Deployment pipelines, **folders are considered part of an item's name** (an item name includes its full path). When an item is deployed, after its path was changed (moved from folder A to folder B, for example), then Deployment pipelines applies this change to its paired item during deployment… **If folder B doesn't exist in the stage we're deploying to, it's created in its workspace first.**\"*\n\nLakehouse1 was moved into `Folder1` **before** the deployment ran, so its full name is now `Folder1\\Lakehouse1`. Workspace2 gets `Folder1` created for it, with Lakehouse1 inside.\n\n**2. Pipeline1 never moved.** It is still at the root of Workspace1, so it deploys to the root of Workspace2 — and it *does* deploy; Data pipelines are a supported item type.\n\nRejected:\n- **D `\\Folder1\\Lakehouse1`** only – drops Pipeline1 entirely. Nothing excluded it from the deployment.\n- **B `\\Pipeline1` `\\Lakehouse1`** – assumes folders are ignored by deployment. The doc says the opposite.\n- **A** – puts Pipeline1 in Folder1 too, but it was never moved there.\n\n*Note:* the vote is a three-way split (C 41 / D 39 / B 20), which is a good sign that the folder rule is worth memorising."
    },
    "sourceVisualReferences": {
      "exhibits": [],
      "answerImages": [],
      "optionImages": []
    },
    "visualResolution": "no_exhibit_needed",
    "refs": [
      {
        "title": "The Fabric deployment pipelines process — folders",
        "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/fabric/cicd/deployment-pipelines/understand-the-deployment-process?wt.mc_id=studentamb_657938"
      }
    ],
    "reviewKind": "original source practice — scientific grading held"
  },
