    "id": "T1Q155",
    "type": "multi",
    "stem": "Your company has a finance department.\nYou have a Fabric tenant, an Azure Storage account named storage1, and a Microsoft Entra group named Group1. Group1 contains the users in the\nfinance department.\nYou need to create a new workspace named Workspace1 in the tenant. The solution must meet the following requirements:\n• Ensure that the finance department users can create and edit items in Workspace1.\n• Ensure that Workspace1 can securely access storage1 to read and write data.\n• Ensure that you are the only admin of Workspace1.\n• Minimize administrative effort.\nYou create Workspace1.\nWhich two actions should you perform next? Each correct answer presents part of the solution.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Assign the Contributor role to Group1."
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Create a workspace identity."
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Assign the Admin role to yourself."
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Assign the Contributor role to each finance department user."
      }
    ],
    "semanticVisuals": [],
    "caseStudy": null,
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q155",
    "sourceId": "T1Q155",
    "gradingEnabled": false,
    "scientificStatus": "R10_APPROVAL_CANDIDATE_NOT_REVALIDATED",
    "r10Status": "APPROVED_WITH_NONBLOCKING_EDITS",
    "reviewNote": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "Four requirements, and two actions cover them:\n\n- **A — assign the Contributor role to Group1.** *\"Finance department users can create and edit items\"* → **Contributor** is the lowest workspace role that can create and edit. Assigning it to **Group1** rather than to individuals satisfies *\"minimize administrative effort\"*: new starters inherit access through group membership with no extra work.\n- **B — create a workspace identity.** *\"Workspace1 can **securely** access storage1 to read and write data\"* → a **workspace identity** is the Microsoft Entra service principal automatically created for the workspace; you grant it a role on `storage1` and Fabric items authenticate with it. No keys, no SAS tokens, no stored credentials — that is the \"securely\" part.\n\nRejected:\n- **C — assign the Admin role to yourself.** Unnecessary: *\"The deploying/creating user automatically becomes … the only admin of the new workspace.\"* You created Workspace1, so you already are its admin — and the requirement is that you remain the **only** one.\n- **D — assign Contributor to each finance user individually.** Same end state as A but the maximum administrative effort, and it drifts out of date as the department changes.",
    "answer": "AB",
    "officialAnswer": "AB",
    "original": {
      "type": "multi",
      "officialAnswer": "AB",
      "answer": "AB",
      "stem": "Your company has a finance department.\nYou have a Fabric tenant, an Azure Storage account named storage1, and a Microsoft Entra group named Group1. Group1 contains the users in the\nfinance department.\nYou need to create a new workspace named Workspace1 in the tenant. The solution must meet the following requirements:\n• Ensure that the finance department users can create and edit items in Workspace1.\n• Ensure that Workspace1 can securely access storage1 to read and write data.\n• Ensure that you are the only admin of Workspace1.\n• Minimize administrative effort.\nYou create Workspace1.\nWhich two actions should you perform next? Each correct answer presents part of the solution.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.",
      "options": [
        {
          "letter": "A",
          "text": "Assign the Contributor role to Group1.",
          "mostVoted": true
        },
        {
          "letter": "B",
          "text": "Create a workspace identity.",
          "mostVoted": true
        },
        {
          "letter": "C",
          "text": "Assign the Admin role to yourself.",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "D",
          "text": "Assign the Contributor role to each finance department user.",
          "mostVoted": false
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "Four requirements, and two actions cover them:\n\n- **A — assign the Contributor role to Group1.** *\"Finance department users can create and edit items\"* → **Contributor** is the lowest workspace role that can create and edit. Assigning it to **Group1** rather than to individuals satisfies *\"minimize administrative effort\"*: new starters inherit access through group membership with no extra work.\n- **B — create a workspace identity.** *\"Workspace1 can **securely** access storage1 to read and write data\"* → a **workspace identity** is the Microsoft Entra service principal automatically created for the workspace; you grant it a role on `storage1` and Fabric items authenticate with it. No keys, no SAS tokens, no stored credentials — that is the \"securely\" part.\n\nRejected:\n- **C — assign the Admin role to yourself.** Unnecessary: *\"The deploying/creating user automatically becomes … the only admin of the new workspace.\"* You created Workspace1, so you already are its admin — and the requirement is that you remain the **only** one.\n- **D — assign Contributor to each finance user individually.** Same end state as A but the maximum administrative effort, and it drifts out of date as the department changes."
    },
