  {
    "id": "T1Q156",
    "type": "mcq",
    "stem": "You have a Fabric tenant that contains the workspaces shown in the following table.\nYou have a deployment pipeline named Pipeline1 that deploys items from Workspace_DEV to Workspace_TEST. In Pipeline1, all items that have\nmatching names are paired.\nYou deploy the contents of Workspace_DEV to Workspace_TEST by using Pipeline1.\nWhat will the contents of Workspace_TEST be once the deployment is complete?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Lakehouse1 - Lakehouse2 - Notebook1 - Notebook2 - Pipeline1 - SemanticModel1"
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Lakehouse1 - Notebook1 - Pipeline1 - SemanticModel1"
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Lakehouse2 - Notebook2 - SemanticModel1"
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Lakehouse2 - Notebook2 - Pipeline1 - SemanticModel1"
      }
    ],
    "semanticVisuals": [
      {
        "kind": "table",
        "title": "Workspaces before deployment",
        "headers": [
          "Workspace",
          "Contents"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "Workspace_DEV",
            "Lakehouse1; Notebook1; Pipeline1; SemanticModel1"
          ],
          [
            "Workspace_TEST",
            "Lakehouse2; Notebook2; SemanticModel1"
          ]
        ]
      }
    ],
    "caseStudy": null,
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q156",
    "sourceId": "T1Q156",
    "gradingEnabled": false,
    "scientificStatus": "R10_APPROVAL_CANDIDATE_NOT_REVALIDATED",
    "r10Status": "APPROVED",
    "reviewNote": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "Deployment **adds and overwrites; it never deletes**. The doc: *\"the items being copied from the source stage overwrite the paired item in the stage you're in according to the pairing rules. **Items that don't exist in the source stage remain as is.**\"*\n\nWork it through. Only items with **matching names** are paired:\n\n| Workspace_DEV | Workspace_TEST (before) | Paired? | Workspace_TEST (after) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Lakehouse1 | — | no | **Lakehouse1** (new) |\n| — | Lakehouse2 | no | Lakehouse2 (untouched) |\n| Notebook1 | — | no | **Notebook1** (new) |\n| — | Notebook2 | no | Notebook2 (untouched) |\n| Pipeline1 | — | no | **Pipeline1** (new) |\n| SemanticModel1 | SemanticModel1 | **yes** | SemanticModel1 (overwritten) |\n\nThe result is the **union**: Lakehouse1, Lakehouse2, Notebook1, Notebook2, Pipeline1, SemanticModel1 — **A**.\n\n- **B** is Workspace_DEV's contents, as if deployment replaced the whole workspace. It does not.\n- **C / D** drop the newly deployed items.\n\n*(Note \"Pipeline1\" here is a **data pipeline item** in Workspace_DEV, distinct from the deployment pipeline doing the deploying — a confusing naming choice in the question, and one commenter is caught by it.)*",
    "answer": "A",
    "officialAnswer": "A",
    "original": {
      "type": "mcq",
      "officialAnswer": "A",
      "answer": "A",
