      ],
      "explanation": "Deployment **adds and overwrites; it never deletes**. The doc: *\"the items being copied from the source stage overwrite the paired item in the stage you're in according to the pairing rules. **Items that don't exist in the source stage remain as is.**\"*\n\nWork it through. Only items with **matching names** are paired:\n\n| Workspace_DEV | Workspace_TEST (before) | Paired? | Workspace_TEST (after) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Lakehouse1 | — | no | **Lakehouse1** (new) |\n| — | Lakehouse2 | no | Lakehouse2 (untouched) |\n| Notebook1 | — | no | **Notebook1** (new) |\n| — | Notebook2 | no | Notebook2 (untouched) |\n| Pipeline1 | — | no | **Pipeline1** (new) |\n| SemanticModel1 | SemanticModel1 | **yes** | SemanticModel1 (overwritten) |\n\nThe result is the **union**: Lakehouse1, Lakehouse2, Notebook1, Notebook2, Pipeline1, SemanticModel1 — **A**.\n\n- **B** is Workspace_DEV's contents, as if deployment replaced the whole workspace. It does not.\n- **C / D** drop the newly deployed items.\n\n*(Note \"Pipeline1\" here is a **data pipeline item** in Workspace_DEV, distinct from the deployment pipeline doing the deploying — a confusing naming choice in the question, and one commenter is caught by it.)*"
