    "explanation": "**Yes — No — No. The PDF answer-key image (No / Yes / Yes) is wrong on all three**, and the documentation settles each one outright.\n\n**1. DF1 (a Dataflow **Gen1**) will be deployed → Yes.** The supported-items list carries two separate entries: **\"Dataflows gen2\"** under *Data Factory items*, and plain **\"Dataflow *(preview)*\"** under *Power BI items* — the latter is Gen1. The dataflow-limitations section confirms Gen1 goes through the pipeline by noting a Gen1-specific caveat: *\"Incremental refresh settings aren't copied in Gen 1.\"* You would not document a copy limitation for an item type that is never deployed.\n\n**2. Data from Model1 will be deployed → No.** From *Item properties that are not copied*: *\"**Data — Data isn't copied. Only metadata is copied**.\"* The same point is made when assigning a workspace: *\"the semantic model refresh is required because **data isn't copied from one stage to another**.\"*\n\n**3. The scheduled refresh policy for Model1 will be deployed → No.** The doc lists the semantic model properties that are **not** copied:\n\n> - Role assignment\n> - **Refresh schedule**\n> - Data source credentials\n> - Query caching settings\n> - Endorsement settings\n\n*(Do not confuse this with the **incremental refresh policy**, which *is* copied: *\"When you deploy the semantic model, the policy is copied along.\"* A refresh **schedule** and an incremental-refresh **policy** are different things.)*\n\n*Community:* the top comment (+21) gives Yes/No/No, and another (+5) reports testing it — *\"I tested and refresh schedule is not deployed: Y,N,N\"*. A third (+11) says No/No/No on the belief that Gen1 dataflows are unsupported, which the supported-items list contradicts.",
