    "id": "T1Q159",
    "type": "hotspot-dropdown",
    "stem": "You have a Fabric tenant that contains a workspace named Workspace1. Workspace1 contains a lakehouse named LH1 and a warehouse named\nDW1. LH1 contains a table named signindata that is in the dbo schema.\nYou need to create a stored procedure in DW1 that deduplicates the data in the signindata table.\nHow should you complete the T-SQL statement? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.",
    "blanks": [
      {
        "label": "CREATE PROCEDURE dbo.usp_GetPerson  AS  ______",
        "options": [
          "BEGIN",
          "BEGIN DISTRIBUTED TRANSACTION",
          "SET"
        ],
        "answer": "BEGIN"
      },
      {
        "label": "SELECT  ______  PersonID, FirstName, LastName",
        "options": [
          "DISTINCT",
          "GROUP BY",
          "TOP (100) PERCENT WITH TIES"
        ],
        "answer": "DISTINCT"
      }
    ],
    "semanticVisuals": [
      {
        "kind": "code",
        "title": "Source stored procedure template",
        "language": "sql",
        "content": "CREATE PROCEDURE dbo.usp_GetPerson\nAS\n[Dropdown 1]\n    SELECT [Dropdown 2] PersonID, FirstName, LastName\n    FROM LH1.dbo.signindata\nEND;"
      }
    ],
    "caseStudy": null,
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q159",
    "sourceId": "T1Q159",
    "gradingEnabled": false,
    "scientificStatus": "BLOCKED_RUNTIME",
    "r10Status": "AMBIGUOUS",
    "reviewNote": "Repaired ambiguous deduplication grain and read-versus-mutation requirement.",
    "remaining": "Read current CREATE PROCEDURE/SELECT docs; execute tuple-grain fixture in Warehouse.",
    "explanation": "**BEGIN — DISTINCT.**\n\n```sql\nCREATE PROCEDURE dbo.usp_GetPerson\nAS\nBEGIN\n    SELECT DISTINCT PersonID, FirstName, LastName\n    FROM LH1.dbo.signindata\nEND\n```\n\n**Blank 1 — `BEGIN`.** A stored procedure body is a `BEGIN … END` block, and the `END` on the last line of the exhibit is its partner.\n- `BEGIN DISTRIBUTED TRANSACTION` starts an MS DTC transaction across servers. This procedure reads one table in one workspace; there is nothing distributed about it, and the closing `END` would have no matching `BEGIN`.\n- `SET` changes a session option (`SET NOCOUNT ON`, …). It is a statement, not a block opener, so `END` would be orphaned.\n\n**Blank 2 — `DISTINCT`.** The requirement is to **deduplicate**, and `SELECT DISTINCT` *\"specifies that only unique rows can appear in the result set\"* — one statement, no extra clauses.\n- `GROUP BY` is not valid there (it follows `FROM`, not `SELECT`). Even placed correctly it would need all three columns restated to achieve the same thing.\n- `TOP (100) PERCENT WITH TIES` returns every row — no deduplication at all (and `WITH TIES` requires an `ORDER BY`).\n\nNote the cross-item read `FROM LH1.dbo.signindata`: a warehouse can query a lakehouse in the same workspace by three-part name.",
    "answer": null,
    "officialAnswer": "",
    "original": {
      "type": "hotspot-dropdown",
      "officialAnswer": "",
      "blanks": [
        {
          "label": "CREATE PROCEDURE dbo.usp_GetPerson  AS  ______",
          "options": [
            "BEGIN",
            "BEGIN DISTRIBUTED TRANSACTION",
            "SET"
          ],
          "answer": "BEGIN"
        },
        {
          "label": "SELECT  ______  PersonID, FirstName, LastName",
          "options": [
            "DISTINCT",
            "GROUP BY",
            "TOP (100) PERCENT WITH TIES"
          ],
          "answer": "DISTINCT"
        }
      ],
      "stem": "You have a Fabric tenant that contains a workspace named Workspace1. Workspace1 contains a lakehouse named LH1 and a warehouse named\nDW1. LH1 contains a table named signindata that is in the dbo schema.\nYou need to create a stored procedure in DW1 that deduplicates the data in the signindata table.\nHow should you complete the T-SQL statement? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.",
      "explanation": "**BEGIN — DISTINCT.**\n\n```sql\nCREATE PROCEDURE dbo.usp_GetPerson\nAS\nBEGIN\n    SELECT DISTINCT PersonID, FirstName, LastName\n    FROM LH1.dbo.signindata\nEND\n```\n\n**Blank 1 — `BEGIN`.** A stored procedure body is a `BEGIN … END` block, and the `END` on the last line of the exhibit is its partner.\n- `BEGIN DISTRIBUTED TRANSACTION` starts an MS DTC transaction across servers. This procedure reads one table in one workspace; there is nothing distributed about it, and the closing `END` would have no matching `BEGIN`.\n- `SET` changes a session option (`SET NOCOUNT ON`, …). It is a statement, not a block opener, so `END` would be orphaned.\n\n**Blank 2 — `DISTINCT`.** The requirement is to **deduplicate**, and `SELECT DISTINCT` *\"specifies that only unique rows can appear in the result set\"* — one statement, no extra clauses.\n- `GROUP BY` is not valid there (it follows `FROM`, not `SELECT`). Even placed correctly it would need all three columns restated to achieve the same thing.\n- `TOP (100) PERCENT WITH TIES` returns every row — no deduplication at all (and `WITH TIES` requires an `ORDER BY`).\n\nNote the cross-item read `FROM LH1.dbo.signindata`: a warehouse can query a lakehouse in the same workspace by three-part name."
    },
