    "explanation": "**Lookup** — the only activity that executes a stored procedure **and** hands its result to later activities: *\"It also returns the result of executing a query or stored procedure. The output can be a singleton value or an array of attributes, which can be consumed in a subsequent copy, transformation, or control flow activity.\"*\n\n- **A Get metadata** – returns metadata about a file or folder (name, size, child items). It executes nothing.\n- **B Switch** – control-flow branching on a value.\n- **D Append variable** – appends to an array variable.\n\n*(Fifth appearance of this item — see T1Q83, T1Q114, T1Q122, T1Q128. Only the distractors change.)*",
