    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "Subtracting two dates in Power Query yields a **duration** value, and `Duration.Days` extracts the whole number of days from it:\n\n```m\nDuration.Days([Shipping_Date] - [Order_Date])\n```\n\n- **C `Duration.From`** – *converts* a value to a duration. It does not give you a day count, and the subtraction has already produced a duration anyway.\n- **D `Date.AddDays`** – shifts a date forward or back by N days. That is the inverse operation.\n- **A `DateTime.LocalNow`** – returns the current local date and time. Nothing to do with the gap between two columns.",
    "answer": "B",
    "officialAnswer": "B",
