    "reviewNote": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "**Tabular Editor.** Object-level security is defined **inside model roles**, and Microsoft states the tooling constraint directly: *\"Like row-level security (RLS), OLS is also defined within model roles. **Currently, you can't create OLS definitions natively in Power BI Desktop.** To create roles on Power BI Desktop semantic models, use external tools such as **Tabular Editor**.\"*\n\n- **B Power BI Desktop** – can create roles and RLS DAX filters, but not OLS.\n- **A the Fabric service** – manages role *membership*, not role definitions.\n- **C ALM Toolkit** – compares and deploys differences between models; it does not author security metadata.\n\n*(T1Q93 is the step-by-step version of the same fact.)*",
    "answer": "D",
    "officialAnswer": "D",
    "original": {
      "type": "mcq",
      "officialAnswer": "D",
      "answer": "D",
      "stem": "You have a Fabric tenant that contains a semantic model.\nYou need to modify object-level security (OLS) for the model.\nWhat should you use?",
