    "id": "T1Q165",
    "type": "mcq",
    "stem": "You have a Microsoft Power BI semantic model that contains a measure named TotalSalesAmount. TotalSalesAmount returns a sales revenue\namount that is translated into a selected currency.\nYou need to ensure that the value returned by TotalSalesAmount is formatted to use the correct currency symbol.\nWhat should you include in the solution?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "a field parameter"
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "a linguistic schema"
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "a dynamic format string"
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "the WINDOW DAX function"
      }
    ],
    "semanticVisuals": [],
    "caseStudy": null,
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q165",
    "sourceId": "T1Q165",
    "gradingEnabled": false,
    "scientificStatus": "R10_APPROVAL_CANDIDATE_NOT_REVALIDATED",
    "r10Status": "APPROVED",
    "reviewNote": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "A **dynamic format string** lets a measure decide its own formatting at evaluation time: *\"With dynamic format strings for measures, you can determine how measures appear in visuals by **conditionally applying a format string with a separate DAX formula**.\"*\n\nThat is exactly the requirement — the measure already returns a value translated into the selected currency, so the format string must follow the same selection:\n\n```dax\nSWITCH (\n    SELECTEDVALUE ( Currency[Code] ),\n    \"USD\", \"$#,##0.00\",\n    \"EUR\", \"€#,##0.00\",\n    \"GBP\", \"£#,##0.00\",\n    \"#,##0.00\"\n)\n```\n\nA static format string on the measure could only ever show one symbol.\n\n- **A a field parameter** – lets report users swap which *fields* a visual shows. It does not control formatting.\n- **B a linguistic schema** – vocabulary for Q&A natural-language queries.\n- **D the WINDOW DAX function** – returns a subset of rows from a table for window calculations. Unrelated to formatting.",
    "answer": "C",
    "officialAnswer": "C",
    "original": {
      "type": "mcq",
      "officialAnswer": "C",
      "answer": "C",
      "stem": "You have a Microsoft Power BI semantic model that contains a measure named TotalSalesAmount. TotalSalesAmount returns a sales revenue\namount that is translated into a selected currency.\nYou need to ensure that the value returned by TotalSalesAmount is formatted to use the correct currency symbol.\nWhat should you include in the solution?",
      "options": [
        {
          "letter": "A",
          "text": "a field parameter",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "B",
          "text": "a linguistic schema",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "C",
          "text": "a dynamic format string",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "D",
          "text": "the WINDOW DAX function",
          "mostVoted": false
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "A **dynamic format string** lets a measure decide its own formatting at evaluation time: *\"With dynamic format strings for measures, you can determine how measures appear in visuals by **conditionally applying a format string with a separate DAX formula**.\"*\n\nThat is exactly the requirement — the measure already returns a value translated into the selected currency, so the format string must follow the same selection:\n\n```dax\nSWITCH (\n    SELECTEDVALUE ( Currency[Code] ),\n    \"USD\", \"$#,##0.00\",\n    \"EUR\", \"€#,##0.00\",\n    \"GBP\", \"£#,##0.00\",\n    \"#,##0.00\"\n)\n```\n\nA static format string on the measure could only ever show one symbol.\n\n- **A a field parameter** – lets report users swap which *fields* a visual shows. It does not control formatting.\n- **B a linguistic schema** – vocabulary for Q&A natural-language queries.\n- **D the WINDOW DAX function** – returns a subset of rows from a table for window calculations. Unrelated to formatting."
    },
