      "stem": "You have a Fabric tenant that contains a workspace named Enterprise. Enterprise contains a semantic model named Model1. Model1 contains a\ndate parameter named Date1 that was created in Power Query.\nYou build a deployment pipeline named Enterprise Data that includes two stages named Development and Test. You assign the Enterprise\nworkspace to the Development stage.\nYou need to perform the following actions:\n• Create a workspace named Enterprise [Test] and assign the workspace to the Test stage.\n• Configure a rule that will modify the value of Date1 when changes are deployed to the Test stage.\nWhich two settings should you use? To answer, select the appropriate settings in the answer area.\nNOTE: Each correct answer is worth one point.",
      "explanation": "Both actions are performed on the **Test** stage, in two different places.\n\n**Creating and assigning the workspace** — the big green control in the empty Test stage reading **\"Deploy to this stage or Assign a workspace\"**. Picking a workspace from its dropdown and selecting *Assign a workspace* attaches `Enterprise [Test]` to the stage. (The *Deploy* button in the Development stage does the other thing — it copies content once a target workspace already exists.)\n\n**Configuring the parameter rule** — the **deployment rules** icon in the Test stage header (the rightmost of the small icons, next to the pencil). Deployment rules are always set on the **target** stage, and `Date1` is a Power Query parameter, so this is a **parameter rule**: *\"Parameter rules … change the value of a parameter\"* on deployment. The doc confirms both parameters and data sources support rules, and that the rule is defined on the stage you deploy *into*.\n\n- The **pencil** icon renames the stage — a commenter guesses this one, but renaming has nothing to do with rules.\n- **Deployment history** and **Manage Access** are pipeline-wide and read-only with respect to rules.\n\n*(This item is an image hotspot on the live exam — you click the two spots on the screenshot. It is transcribed here as two dropdowns.)*"
