      "stem": "You have a Fabric workspace named Workspace1 that uses the Premium Per User (PPU) license mode and contains a semantic model named\nModel1.\nLarge semantic model storage format is selected for Model1.\nYou need to ensure that tables imported into Model1 are written automatically to Delta tables in OneLake.\nWhat should you do for Model1 and Workspace1? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.",
      "explanation": "**Model1 → Enable OneLake integration. Workspace1 → Change the license mode to Fabric capacity.**\n\n### Model1 — the feature has a name, and it is in the requirement\n\nThe requirement — *\"tables imported into Model1 are written automatically to Delta tables in OneLake\"* — is a verbatim paraphrase of the feature description: *\"With Microsoft OneLake integration for semantic models, **data imported into model tables can also be automatically written to Delta tables in OneLake**.\"* You turn it on per model: **Semantic model settings → OneLake integration → On → Apply**.\n\n- **Enable query caching** ✘ — caches query *results* in the capacity to speed up report loads. Reads, not exports.\n- **Enable query scale-out** ✘ — spins up read-only model replicas so heavy reporting does not collide with refreshes. Again a read-path feature; it writes nothing to OneLake.\n\n### Workspace1 — PPU is the trap\n\nThe stem tells you Workspace1 uses **Premium Per User**, and then tells you Large semantic model storage format is already selected. That second sentence is there to reassure you the *model-side* prerequisite is already met, leaving the *capacity-side* one as the gap:\n\n> **\"OneLake integration for semantic models is supported on Power BI Premium P and Microsoft Fabric F SKUs only. It's not supported on Power BI Pro, Premium Per User, or Power BI Embedded A/EM SKUs.\"**\n\nSo the workspace has to move off PPU onto a Fabric (F SKU) capacity. Nothing else in the list is a licensing change:\n\n- **Create a workspace identity** ✘ — a managed identity used for trusted-workspace access to firewall-protected ADLS Gen2 storage. Outbound authentication, not licensing.\n- **Enable authentication by using OneLake user-delegated SAS tokens** ✘ — lets applications mint short-lived SAS tokens for OneLake data access. An access-control feature for external callers.\n\n*(One commenter suggests \"Direct Lake mode\" for the first blank. It is not on the option list, and it would be the wrong idea anyway: Direct Lake **reads** Delta tables that already exist in OneLake. This question is the opposite direction — **exporting** an import model's tables *into* OneLake as Delta.)*\n\n**Remember the two prerequisites together: Large semantic model storage format + a P/F capacity.** After enabling, at least one manual or scheduled refresh must run before the Delta tables appear."
