    "id": "T1Q192",
    "type": "mcq",
    "stem": "You have a Fabric tenant that contains the workspaces shown in the following table.\nYou have a deployment pipeline named Pipeline1 that deploys items from Workspace_DEV to Workspace_TEST. In Pipeline1, all items that have\nmatching names are paired.\nYou deploy the contents of Workspace_DEV to Workspace_TEST by using Pipeline1.\nWhat will the contents of Workspace_TEST be once the deployment is complete?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Lakehouse2 - Notebook2 - SemanticModel1 -"
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Lakehouse1 - Notebook1 - Pipeline1 - SemanticModel1 -"
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Lakehouse1 - Lakehouse2 - Notebook1 - Notebook2 - Pipeline1 - SemanticModel1 -"
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Lakehouse2 - Notebook2 - Pipeline1 - SemanticModel1"
      }
    ],
    "semanticVisuals": [
      {
        "kind": "table",
        "title": "Workspaces before deployment",
        "headers": [
          "Workspace",
          "Contents"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "Workspace_DEV",
            "Lakehouse1; Notebook1; Pipeline1; SemanticModel1"
          ],
          [
            "Workspace_TEST",
            "Lakehouse2; Notebook2; SemanticModel1"
          ]
        ]
      }
    ],
    "caseStudy": null,
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q192",
    "sourceId": "T1Q192",
    "gradingEnabled": false,
    "scientificStatus": "R10_APPROVAL_CANDIDATE_NOT_REVALIDATED",
    "r10Status": "APPROVED",
    "reviewNote": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "**C — Lakehouse1, Lakehouse2, Notebook1, Notebook2, Pipeline1, SemanticModel1.**\n\n| | Workspace_DEV (before) | Workspace_TEST (before) | Workspace_TEST (after) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| | Lakehouse1 | Lakehouse2 | Lakehouse1 *(new)* |\n| | Notebook1 | Notebook2 | Lakehouse2 *(untouched)* |\n| | Pipeline1 | SemanticModel1 | Notebook1 *(new)* |\n| | SemanticModel1 | | Notebook2 *(untouched)* |\n| | | | Pipeline1 *(new)* |\n| | | | SemanticModel1 *(paired → overwritten)* |\n\nTwo rules produce this, and the distractors each break one of them:\n\n**1. Deployment is additive, not a mirror.** Deploying copies the source stage's items forward; it **does not delete** items that exist only in the target. Lakehouse2 and Notebook2 have no counterpart in DEV, so they simply stay. This kills **A** and **D**, which both drop Lakehouse1 and Notebook1 — and it is the single most-tested fact about deployment pipelines.\n\n**2. Matching names are paired and overwritten, not duplicated.** SemanticModel1 exists in both stages and is paired, so the DEV copy overwrites the TEST one — you end up with **one** SemanticModel1, not two. (Pairing is by item **name and type**; an unpaired item is created fresh in the target.)\n\n**B** fails rule 1 in the other direction — it lists only what came from DEV and silently deletes Lakehouse2 and Notebook2.\n\n*Read `Pipeline1` carefully:* there are two different things called Pipeline1 here — the **deployment pipeline** doing the work, and a **data pipeline item** sitting in Workspace_DEV's contents list. It is the latter that gets deployed. Deployment pipelines are not workspace items and never deploy themselves.\n\n*(Duplicate of T1Q156 — identical scenario and answer.)*",
    "answer": "C",
    "officialAnswer": "C",
    "original": {
      "type": "mcq",
      "officialAnswer": "C",
      "answer": "C",
      "stem": "You have a Fabric tenant that contains the workspaces shown in the following table.\nYou have a deployment pipeline named Pipeline1 that deploys items from Workspace_DEV to Workspace_TEST. In Pipeline1, all items that have\nmatching names are paired.\nYou deploy the contents of Workspace_DEV to Workspace_TEST by using Pipeline1.\nWhat will the contents of Workspace_TEST be once the deployment is complete?",
      "options": [
