  {
    "id": "T1Q200",
    "type": "multi",
    "stem": "You have a Fabric workspace named Workspace1 that contains a lakehouse named Lakehouse1 and a user named User1.\nYou need to ensure that User1 can read all the data in Lakehouse1. The solution must follow the principle of least privilege.\nWhich two actions should you perform? Each correct answer presents part of the solution.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Assign the Contributor role to User1."
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Select Read all Apache Spark."
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Assign the Viewer role to User1."
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Share Lakehouse1 by using item permissions."
      },
      {
        "letter": "E",
        "text": "Assign the Member role to User1."
      }
    ],
    "semanticVisuals": [],
    "caseStudy": null,
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q200",
    "sourceId": "T1Q200",
    "gradingEnabled": false,
    "scientificStatus": "R10_APPROVAL_CANDIDATE_NOT_REVALIDATED",
    "r10Status": "APPROVED",
    "reviewNote": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "**B + D — share Lakehouse1 by using item permissions, and select \"Read all Apache Spark\".**\n\nTwo decisions, one per answer.\n\n**D — *how* to grant: item permissions, not a workspace role.** This is what *\"principle of least privilege\"* is testing. A workspace role applies to **every item in Workspace1**; item-level sharing applies to **Lakehouse1 alone**. Since the requirement names exactly one lakehouse, sharing the item is the narrowest grant that does the job.\n\n**B — *what* to grant: ReadAll (\"Read all Apache Spark\").** The requirement is *\"read **all the data**\"*, and in a lakehouse the data is the OneLake files and Delta tables. **ReadAll** is the permission that opens them:\n\n| Sharing checkbox | Permission | Grants |\n|---|---|---|\n| *(none — always granted)* | Read | connect to the SQL analytics endpoint only |\n| \"Read all SQL endpoint data\" | ReadData | `SELECT` on tables/views through the SQL endpoint |\n| **\"Read all Apache Spark\"** | **ReadAll** | **read all files and Delta tables in OneLake** (Spark, notebooks, shortcuts) |\n| \"Build reports on the default semantic model\" | Build | build reports on the default semantic model |\n\nSharing with no boxes ticked would give User1 only `CONNECT` — enough to reach the endpoint, not enough to read anything (see T1Q193).\n\nWhy the role options fail:\n\n- **C Viewer** ✘ — the tempting \"read-only\" choice. Viewer *is* the least-privileged **role**, but a role is workspace-wide: User1 would gain read access to every current and future item in Workspace1, not just Lakehouse1. Broader than required.\n- **A Contributor** ✘ and **E Member** ✘ — both grant **write** access to the whole workspace, and Member can also add other users. Wildly beyond \"read\".\n\n**Rule: when a question names one item and says \"least privilege\", reach for item permissions (Share), not a workspace role.**",
    "answer": "BD",
    "officialAnswer": "BD",
    "original": {
      "type": "multi",
      "officialAnswer": "BD",
      "answer": "BD",
      "stem": "You have a Fabric workspace named Workspace1 that contains a lakehouse named Lakehouse1 and a user named User1.\nYou need to ensure that User1 can read all the data in Lakehouse1. The solution must follow the principle of least privilege.\nWhich two actions should you perform? Each correct answer presents part of the solution.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.",
      "options": [
        {
          "letter": "A",
          "text": "Assign the Contributor role to User1.",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "B",
          "text": "Select Read all Apache Spark.",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "C",
          "text": "Assign the Viewer role to User1.",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "D",
          "text": "Share Lakehouse1 by using item permissions.",
          "mostVoted": false
        },
        {
          "letter": "E",
          "text": "Assign the Member role to User1.",
          "mostVoted": false
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "**B + D — share Lakehouse1 by using item permissions, and select \"Read all Apache Spark\".**\n\nTwo decisions, one per answer.\n\n**D — *how* to grant: item permissions, not a workspace role.** This is what *\"principle of least privilege\"* is testing. A workspace role applies to **every item in Workspace1**; item-level sharing applies to **Lakehouse1 alone**. Since the requirement names exactly one lakehouse, sharing the item is the narrowest grant that does the job.\n\n**B — *what* to grant: ReadAll (\"Read all Apache Spark\").** The requirement is *\"read **all the data**\"*, and in a lakehouse the data is the OneLake files and Delta tables. **ReadAll** is the permission that opens them:\n\n| Sharing checkbox | Permission | Grants |\n|---|---|---|\n| *(none — always granted)* | Read | connect to the SQL analytics endpoint only |\n| \"Read all SQL endpoint data\" | ReadData | `SELECT` on tables/views through the SQL endpoint |\n| **\"Read all Apache Spark\"** | **ReadAll** | **read all files and Delta tables in OneLake** (Spark, notebooks, shortcuts) |\n| \"Build reports on the default semantic model\" | Build | build reports on the default semantic model |\n\nSharing with no boxes ticked would give User1 only `CONNECT` — enough to reach the endpoint, not enough to read anything (see T1Q193).\n\nWhy the role options fail:\n\n- **C Viewer** ✘ — the tempting \"read-only\" choice. Viewer *is* the least-privileged **role**, but a role is workspace-wide: User1 would gain read access to every current and future item in Workspace1, not just Lakehouse1. Broader than required.\n- **A Contributor** ✘ and **E Member** ✘ — both grant **write** access to the whole workspace, and Member can also add other users. Wildly beyond \"read\".\n\n**Rule: when a question names one item and says \"least privilege\", reach for item permissions (Share), not a workspace role.**"
