  {
    "id": "T1Q209",
    "type": "hotspot-dropdown",
    "stem": "You have a Microsoft Entra tenant named contoso.com and an external user named user1@fabrikam.com .\nYou have a Fabric workspace named Workspace1 that contains a semantic model named Model1 and a report named Report1.\nUser1@fabrikam.com has access to Report1.\nYou enable read-write on the XML for Analysis (XMLA) endpoint to provide advanced semantic modeling by using DAX Studio.\nYou need to provide user1@fabrikam.com with a URL that will enable connectivity by using DAX Studio.\nHow should you complete the URL? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.",
    "blanks": [
      {
        "label": "powerbi://api.powerbi.com/v1.0/[answer choice]",
        "options": [
          "common",
          "contoso.com",
          "fabrikam.com",
          "myorg"
        ],
        "answer": "contoso.com"
      },
      {
        "label": "/[answer choice]",
        "options": [
          "Model1",
          "Report1",
          "Workspace1"
        ],
        "answer": "Workspace1"
      }
    ],
    "semanticVisuals": [
      {
        "kind": "code",
        "title": "Original XMLA endpoint completion template",
        "language": "text",
        "content": "powerbi://api.powerbi.com/v1.0/[Dropdown 1]/[Dropdown 2]"
      }
    ],
    "caseStudy": null,
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q209",
    "sourceId": "T1Q209",
    "gradingEnabled": false,
    "scientificStatus": "R10_APPROVAL_CANDIDATE_NOT_REVALIDATED",
    "r10Status": "APPROVED_WITH_NONBLOCKING_EDITS",
    "reviewNote": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "**`powerbi://api.powerbi.com/v1.0/contoso.com/Workspace1`**\n\n### Blank 1 — `contoso.com`, not `myorg`\n\nThe XMLA endpoint URL is `powerbi://api.powerbi.com/v1.0/<tenant>/<workspace name>`, and the `<tenant>` segment is the whole point of this question:\n\n| Segment | When to use it |\n|---|---|\n| `myorg` | the **default alias for your own home tenant** — works for internal users signing in to their own organisation |\n| **`contoso.com`** | the **explicit tenant name of the organisation that owns the workspace** — required for **guest / B2B** users |\n\n`user1@fabrikam.com` is an **external user** in contoso.com's Entra tenant. If they used `myorg`, the service would resolve it to *fabrikam.com* — their own home tenant — and the workspace would not be found. Guest users must name the **host** tenant explicitly, so the URL has to say `contoso.com`.\n\n- **`fabrikam.com`** ✘ — the user's own tenant. Workspace1 does not live there. This is the trap the question is built around: the domain in the URL is the **owner's**, never the guest's.\n- **`common`** ✘ — a Microsoft Entra *authentication* endpoint alias (`login.microsoftonline.com/common`), used for multi-tenant sign-in. It is not a Power BI workspace path segment.\n\n### Blank 2 — `Workspace1`\n\nThe XMLA endpoint addresses a **workspace**, which DAX Studio and SSMS treat as an Analysis Services *server*. Once connected, the semantic models inside it appear as *databases* — so you select `Model1` **after** connecting, from the database dropdown.\n\n- **`Model1`** ✘ — a database within the server, not part of the server URL.\n- **`Report1`** ✘ — reports are not addressable over XMLA at all; the endpoint exposes semantic models only.\n\n**Remember: XMLA connects to a *workspace*; the workspace is the server, the semantic models are its databases. And `myorg` only means \"my org\" for members of that org — guests must spell the tenant out.**",
    "answer": null,
    "officialAnswer": "",
    "original": {
      "type": "hotspot-dropdown",
      "officialAnswer": "",
      "blanks": [
        {
          "label": "powerbi://api.powerbi.com/v1.0/[answer choice]",
          "options": [
            "common",
            "contoso.com",
            "fabrikam.com",
            "myorg"
          ],
          "answer": "contoso.com"
        },
        {
          "label": "/[answer choice]",
          "options": [
            "Model1",
            "Report1",
            "Workspace1"
          ],
          "answer": "Workspace1"
        }
      ],
      "stem": "You have a Microsoft Entra tenant named contoso.com and an external user named user1@fabrikam.com .\nYou have a Fabric workspace named Workspace1 that contains a semantic model named Model1 and a report named Report1.\nUser1@fabrikam.com has access to Report1.\nYou enable read-write on the XML for Analysis (XMLA) endpoint to provide advanced semantic modeling by using DAX Studio.\nYou need to provide user1@fabrikam.com with a URL that will enable connectivity by using DAX Studio.\nHow should you complete the URL? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.",
      "explanation": "**`powerbi://api.powerbi.com/v1.0/contoso.com/Workspace1`**\n\n### Blank 1 — `contoso.com`, not `myorg`\n\nThe XMLA endpoint URL is `powerbi://api.powerbi.com/v1.0/<tenant>/<workspace name>`, and the `<tenant>` segment is the whole point of this question:\n\n| Segment | When to use it |\n|---|---|\n| `myorg` | the **default alias for your own home tenant** — works for internal users signing in to their own organisation |\n| **`contoso.com`** | the **explicit tenant name of the organisation that owns the workspace** — required for **guest / B2B** users |\n\n`user1@fabrikam.com` is an **external user** in contoso.com's Entra tenant. If they used `myorg`, the service would resolve it to *fabrikam.com* — their own home tenant — and the workspace would not be found. Guest users must name the **host** tenant explicitly, so the URL has to say `contoso.com`.\n\n- **`fabrikam.com`** ✘ — the user's own tenant. Workspace1 does not live there. This is the trap the question is built around: the domain in the URL is the **owner's**, never the guest's.\n- **`common`** ✘ — a Microsoft Entra *authentication* endpoint alias (`login.microsoftonline.com/common`), used for multi-tenant sign-in. It is not a Power BI workspace path segment.\n\n### Blank 2 — `Workspace1`\n\nThe XMLA endpoint addresses a **workspace**, which DAX Studio and SSMS treat as an Analysis Services *server*. Once connected, the semantic models inside it appear as *databases* — so you select `Model1` **after** connecting, from the database dropdown.\n\n- **`Model1`** ✘ — a database within the server, not part of the server URL.\n- **`Report1`** ✘ — reports are not addressable over XMLA at all; the endpoint exposes semantic models only.\n\n**Remember: XMLA connects to a *workspace*; the workspace is the server, the semantic models are its databases. And `myorg` only means \"my org\" for members of that org — guests must spell the tenant out.**"
    },
