  {
    "id": "T1Q217",
    "type": "mcq",
    "stem": "You have a Fabric workspace named Workspace1 and a user named User1.\nYou need to ensure that User1 can perform the following tasks in Workspace1:\n• Create dashboards.\n• Publish semantic models.\n• Create and publish reports.\nThe solution must follow the principle of least privilege.\nWhich workspace role should you assign to User1?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Contributor"
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Member"
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Viewer"
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Admin"
      }
    ],
    "semanticVisuals": [],
    "caseStudy": null,
    "hansaId": "new-json-t1q217",
    "sourceId": "T1Q217",
    "gradingEnabled": false,
    "scientificStatus": "R10_APPROVAL_CANDIDATE_NOT_REVALIDATED",
    "r10Status": "APPROVED",
    "reviewNote": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "remaining": "R11 second-pass review not performed; retained R10 finding is a lead, not new verification.",
    "explanation": "**A — Contributor.** Walk the three tasks down the role ladder and find the lowest rung that clears all of them:\n\n| Task | Viewer | **Contributor** | Member | Admin |\n|---|:-:|:-:|:-:|:-:|\n| Create dashboards | ✘ | **✔** | ✔ | ✔ |\n| Publish semantic models | ✘ | **✔** | ✔ | ✔ |\n| Create and publish reports | ✘ | **✔** | ✔ | ✔ |\n| *(not required)* Add members / share items | ✘ | ✘ | ✔ | ✔ |\n| *(not required)* Update or delete the workspace | ✘ | ✘ | ✘ | ✔ |\n\nAll three requirements are **create-and-publish content** operations, which is exactly what Contributor is defined to allow: create, edit and delete items in the workspace, publish reports and semantic models, schedule refreshes.\n\n- **C Viewer** ✘ — read-only. Can open reports and dashboards; cannot create or publish anything.\n- **B Member** ✘ — clears all three, but also adds the right to **share items and add other users**. Nothing in the requirements asks for that, so it fails least privilege.\n- **D Admin** ✘ — clears all three, and can also delete the workspace and manage all access. Furthest from least privilege.\n\n**The decision rule for every Fabric role question: list what the user must *do*, find the smallest role that covers all of it, and stop.** Contributor is the answer whenever the tasks are all \"make and publish content\"; Member becomes necessary the moment \"share with others\" or \"add users\" appears (see T1Q210, T1Q172).",
    "answer": "A",
    "officialAnswer": "A",
    "original": {
      "type": "mcq",
      "officialAnswer": "A",
      "answer": "A",
      "stem": "You have a Fabric workspace named Workspace1 and a user named User1.\nYou need to ensure that User1 can perform the following tasks in Workspace1:\n• Create dashboards.\n• Publish semantic models.\n• Create and publish reports.\nThe solution must follow the principle of least privilege.\nWhich workspace role should you assign to User1?",
      "options": [
